#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-buffer_002dname\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-buffer_002dfile_002dname\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-buffer_002dname\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-buffer_002dfile_002dname\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The two functions, <code class=\"code\">buffer-name</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">buffer-file-name</code>, show the difference between a file "
"and a buffer.  When you evaluate the following expression, <code "
"class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</code>, the name of the buffer appears in the "
"echo area.  When you evaluate <code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</"
"code>, the name of the file to which the buffer refers appears in the echo "
"area.  Usually, the name returned by <code class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</"
"code> is the same as the name of the file to which it refers, and the name "
"returned by <code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code> is the full path-"
"name of the file."
msgstr ""
"2つの関数 <code class=\"code\">buffer-name</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">buffer-file-name</code> は、ファイルとバッファの違いを示しま"
"す。次の式 <code class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</code> を評価すると、バッファの"
"名前がエコーエリアに表示されます。<code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</"
"code> を評価すると、バッファが参照するファイルの名前がエコーエリアに表示され"
"ます。通常、<code class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</code> が返す名前はそれが参照"
"するファイルの名前と同じであり、<code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</"
"code> が返す名前はファイルのフルパス名となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A file and a buffer are two different entities.  A file is information "
"recorded permanently in the computer (unless you delete it).  A buffer, on "
"the other hand, is information inside of Emacs that will vanish at the end "
"of the editing session (or when you kill the buffer).  Usually, a buffer "
"contains information that you have copied from a file; we say the buffer is "
"<em class=\"dfn\">visiting</em> that file.  This copy is what you work on "
"and modify.  Changes to the buffer do not change the file, until you save "
"the buffer.  When you save the buffer, the buffer is copied to the file and "
"is thus saved permanently."
msgstr ""
"ファイルとバッファは、それぞれ異なるものです。ファイルとは、コンピュータに永"
"続的に記録された情報のことです（削除しない限り）。一方、バッファとはEmacs内部"
"にある情報であり、編集セッションの終了時（またはバッファを破棄したとき）に消"
"滅します。通常、バッファにはファイルからコピーした情報が含まれており、このと"
"きバッファはそのファイルを<em class=\"dfn\">参照</em>していると言います。この"
"コピーこそが、作業や修正の対象となるものです。バッファへの変更は、バッファを"
"保存するまでファイルには反映されません。バッファを保存すると、バッファの内容"
"がファイルにコピーされ、それによって永続的に保存されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If you are reading this in Info inside of GNU Emacs, you can evaluate each "
"of the following expressions by positioning the cursor after it and typing "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"GNU EmacsのInfoでこれを読んでいる場合は、以下の各式の後にカーソルを置き、"
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd>と入力することで評価できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(buffer-name)\n"
"\n"
"(buffer-file-name)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When I do this in Info, the value returned by evaluating <code "
"class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</code> is <samp "
"class=\"file\">&quot;*info*&quot;</samp>, and the value returned by "
"evaluating <code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code> is <samp "
"class=\"file\">nil</samp>."
msgstr ""
"Infoでこれを行うと、<code class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</code>を評価して返され"
"る値は<samp class=\"file\">&quot;*info*&quot;</samp>となり、<code "
"class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code>を評価して返される値は<samp "
"class=\"file\">nil</samp>となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"On the other hand, while I am writing this document, the value returned by "
"evaluating <code class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</code> is <samp "
"class=\"file\">&quot;introduction.texinfo&quot;</samp>, and the value "
"returned by evaluating <code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code> is "
"<samp class=\"file\">&quot;/gnu/work/intro/introduction.texinfo&quot;</samp>."
msgstr ""
"一方で、この文書を書いている時点では、<code class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</"
"code>を評価して返される値は<samp "
"class=\"file\">&quot;introduction.texinfo&quot;</samp>であり、<code "
"class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code>を評価して返される値は<samp "
"class=\"file\">&quot;/gnu/work/intro/introduction.texinfo&quot;</samp>です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-nil_002c-history-of-word\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-nil_002c-history-of-word\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The former is the name of the buffer and the latter is the name of the "
"file.  In Info, the buffer name is <samp class=\"file\">&quot;*info*&quot;</"
"samp>.  Info does not point to any file, so the result of evaluating <code "
"class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code> is <samp class=\"file\">nil</"
"samp>.  The symbol <code class=\"code\">nil</code> is from the Latin word "
"for &ldquo;nothing&rdquo;; in this case, it means that the buffer is not "
"associated with any file.  (In Lisp, <code class=\"code\">nil</code> is also "
"used to mean &ldquo;false&rdquo; and is a synonym for the empty list, <code "
"class=\"code\">()</code>.)"
msgstr ""
"前者はバッファ名、後者はファイル名です。Infoでは、バッファ名は<samp "
"class=\"file\">&quot;*info*&quot;</samp>となります。Infoはいかなるファイルも"
"指していないため、<code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code>を評価した結"
"果は<samp class=\"file\">nil</samp>となります。記号<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>はラテン語の「何もない」に由来しており、この場合はバッファがいかなるファ"
"イルとも関連付けられていないことを意味します。（Lispでは、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>も「偽」という意味で用いられ、空リスト<code "
"class=\"code\">()</code>の同義語となります。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When I am writing, the name of my buffer is <samp "
"class=\"file\">&quot;introduction.texinfo&quot;</samp>.  The name of the "
"file to which it points is <samp class=\"file\">&quot;/gnu/work/intro/"
"introduction.texinfo&quot;</samp>."
msgstr ""
"書き込み中のバッファ名は<samp class=\"file\">&quot;introduction.texinfo&quot;"
"</samp>です。それが指しているファイルの名前は<samp class=\"file\">&quot;/gnu/"
"work/intro/introduction.texinfo&quot;</samp>です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html
msgid ""
"(In the expressions, the parentheses tell the Lisp interpreter to treat "
"<code class=\"code\">buffer-name</code> and <code class=\"code\">buffer-file-"
"name</code> as functions; without the parentheses, the interpreter would "
"attempt to evaluate the symbols as variables.  See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Variables.html\">Variables</a>.)"
msgstr ""
"（式中の括弧は、Lispインタプリタに <code class=\"code\">buffer-name</code> "
"と <code class=\"code\">buffer-file-name</code> を関数として扱うよう指示する"
"ものです。括弧がない場合、インタプリタはこれらのシンボルを変数として評価しよ"
"うとします。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Variables.html\">変数</a>を参照してくだ"
"さい。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In spite of the distinction between files and buffers, you will often find "
"that people refer to a file when they mean a buffer and vice versa.  Indeed, "
"most people say, &ldquo;I am editing a file,&rdquo; rather than saying, "
"&ldquo;I am editing a buffer which I will soon save to a file.&rdquo; It is "
"almost always clear from context what people mean.  When dealing with "
"computer programs, however, it is important to keep the distinction in mind, "
"since the computer is not as smart as a person."
msgstr ""
"ファイルとバッファの区別はあるものの、バッファのことを指してファイルと言った"
"り、その逆を言ったりする場面によく遭遇します。実際、ほとんどの人は「まもなく"
"ファイルに保存するバッファを編集している」と言うのではなく、「ファイルを編集"
"している」と言います。文脈からすれば、相手が何を意味しているのかはほぼ常に明"
"確です。しかし、コンピュータプログラムを扱う際には、コンピュータは人間ほど賢"
"くないため、この区別を念頭に置いておくことが重要です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Buffer_002c-history-of-word\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Buffer_002c-history-of-word\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The word &ldquo;buffer&rdquo;, by the way, comes from the meaning of the "
"word as a cushion that deadens the force of a collision.  In early "
"computers, a buffer cushioned the interaction between files and the "
"computer&rsquo;s central processing unit.  The drums or tapes that held a "
"file and the central processing unit were pieces of equipment that were very "
"different from each other, working at their own speeds, in spurts.  The "
"buffer made it possible for them to work together effectively.  Eventually, "
"the buffer grew from being an intermediary, a temporary holding place, to "
"being the place where work is done.  This transformation is rather like that "
"of a small seaport that grew into a great city: once it was merely the place "
"where cargo was warehoused temporarily before being loaded onto ships; then "
"it became a business and cultural center in its own right."
msgstr ""
"ちなみに、「バッファ」という言葉は、衝突の衝撃を和らげるクッションという意味"
"に由来しています。初期のコンピュータにおいて、バッファはファイルとコンピュー"
"タの中央処理装置とのやり取りを緩衝する役割を果たしていました。ファイルを保持"
"するドラムやテープと、中央処理装置は、それぞれ動作速度が異なり、断続的に動作"
"する、全く性質の異なる装置でした。バッファがあることで、これらが効果的に連携"
"することが可能になったのです。やがてバッファは、仲介役や一時的な保管場所か"
"ら、実際に処理が行われる場所へと発展していきました。この変遷は、小さな港町が"
"大都市へと成長した過程に似ています。かつては単に、船に積み込まれる前に貨物を"
"一時的に保管する場所に過ぎませんでしたが、やがてそれ自体が商業・文化の中心地"
"となったのです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Not all buffers are associated with files.  For example, a <samp "
"class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> buffer does not visit any file.  Similarly, "
"a <samp class=\"file\">*Help*</samp> buffer is not associated with any file."
msgstr ""
"すべてのバッファがファイルに関連付けられているわけではありません。例えば、"
"<samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> バッファはどのファイルにもアクセスしま"
"せん。同様に、<samp class=\"file\">*Help*</samp> バッファもどのファイルにも関"
"連付けられていません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In the old days, when you lacked a <samp class=\"file\">~/.emacs</samp> file "
"and started an Emacs session by typing the command <code "
"class=\"code\">emacs</code> alone, without naming any files, Emacs started "
"with the <samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> buffer visible.  Nowadays, "
"you will see a splash screen.  You can follow one of the commands suggested "
"on the splash screen, visit a file, or press <kbd class=\"kbd\">q</kbd> to "
"quit the splash screen and reach the <samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> "
"buffer."
msgstr ""
"昔は、<samp class=\"file\">~/.emacs</samp> ファイルがなく、ファイル名を指定せ"
"ずに <code class=\"code\">emacs</code> コマンドだけを入力して Emacs を起動す"
"ると、<samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> バッファが表示された状態で Emacs "
"が起動していました。現在では、スプラッシュ画面が表示されます。スプラッシュ画"
"面に表示されているコマンドのいずれかを実行するか、ファイルを開くか、あるいは "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">q</kbd> を押してスプラッシュ画面を終了し、<samp "
"class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> バッファに移動することができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If you switch to the <samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> buffer, type "
"<code class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</code>, position the cursor after it, and "
"then type <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd> to evaluate the expression.  The "
"name <code class=\"code\">&quot;*scratch*&quot;</code> will be returned and "
"will appear in the echo area.  <code class=\"code\">&quot;*scratch*&quot;</"
"code> is the name of the buffer.  When you type <code class=\"code\">(buffer-"
"file-name)</code> in the <samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> buffer and "
"evaluate that, <code class=\"code\">nil</code> will appear in the echo area, "
"just as it does when you evaluate <code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</"
"code> in Info."
msgstr ""
"<samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> バッファに切り替え、<code "
"class=\"code\">(buffer-name)</code> と入力してその後ろにカーソルを置き、さら"
"に <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd> と入力して式を評価します。<code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;*scratch*&quot;</code> という名前が返され、エコーエリア"
"に表示されます。<code class=\"code\">&quot;*scratch*&quot;</code> はバッファ"
"の名前です。<samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> バッファで <code "
"class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code> と入力してそれを評価すると、Info で "
"<code class=\"code\">(buffer-file-name)</code> を評価したときと同様に、<code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> がエコーエリアに表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Incidentally, if you are in the <samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> buffer "
"and want the value returned by an expression to appear in the <samp "
"class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> buffer itself rather than in the echo area, "
"type <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-u C-x C-e</kbd> instead of <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x "
"C-e</kbd>.  This causes the value returned to appear after the expression.  "
"The buffer will look like this:"
msgstr ""
"ちなみに、<samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> バッファにいて、式が返す値を"
"エコー領域ではなく <samp class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> バッファ自体に表示さ"
"せたい場合は、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd> ではなく <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-"
"u C-x C-e</kbd> と入力してください。これにより、式の後に返された値が表示され"
"るようになります。バッファは次のようになります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(buffer-name)&quot;*scratch*&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Buffer-Names.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You cannot do this in Info since Info is read-only and it will not allow you "
"to change the contents of the buffer.  But you can do this in any buffer you "
"can edit; and when you write code or documentation (such as this book), this "
"feature is very useful."
msgstr ""
"Infoは読み取り専用であり、バッファの内容を変更することはできないため、Infoで"
"はこのような操作はできません。しかし、編集可能なバッファであればどれでも同様"
"の操作が可能です。また、コードやドキュメント（本書など）を作成する際、この機"
"能は非常に重宝します。"

