# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Building-Robots.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"It is sometimes helpful to think of a running program as a robot that does a "
"job.  In doing its job, a recursive function calls on a second robot to help "
"it.  The second robot is identical to the first in every way, except that "
"the second robot helps the first and has been passed different arguments "
"than the first."
msgstr ""
"実行中のプログラムを、仕事をこなすロボットとして捉えると分かりやすいことがあ"
"ります。再帰関数は仕事を行う際、補助として2台目のロボットを呼び出します。この"
"2台目のロボットは、1台目のロボットを助けるという点と、1台目とは異なる引数が渡"
"されている点を除けば、あらゆる面で1台目と同一です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Building-Robots.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In a recursive function, the second robot may call a third; and the third "
"may call a fourth, and so on.  Each of these is a different entity; but all "
"are clones."
msgstr ""
"再帰関数において、2台目のロボットが3台目を呼び出し、3台目が4台目を呼び出す、"
"といった具合に続く。これらはそれぞれ異なる個体だが、すべてクローンである。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Building-Robots.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Since each robot has slightly different instructions&mdash;the arguments "
"will differ from one robot to the next&mdash;the last robot should know when "
"to stop."
msgstr ""
"ロボットごとに指示がわずかに異なるため&mdash;引数もロボットごとに異なります"
"&mdash;最後のロボットは、いつ停止すべきかを判断できる必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Building-Robots.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Let&rsquo;s expand on the metaphor in which a computer program is a robot."
msgstr ""
"コンピュータプログラムをロボットとする比喩について、詳しく見ていきましょう。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Building-Robots.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A function definition provides the blueprints for a robot.  When you install "
"a function definition, that is, when you evaluate a <code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code> macro, you install the necessary equipment to "
"build robots.  It is as if you were in a factory, setting up an assembly "
"line.  Robots with the same name are built according to the same "
"blueprints.  So they have the same model number, but a different serial "
"number."
msgstr ""
"関数定義は、ロボットの設計図となります。関数定義をインストールする、つまり"
"<code class=\"code\">defun</code>マクロを評価すると、ロボットを製造するために"
"必要な設備が導入されます。それはまるで工場で、組立ラインをセットアップしてい"
"るかのようです。同じ名前のロボットは、同じ設計図に基づいて製造されます。その"
"ため、モデル番号は同じですが、シリアル番号は異なります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Building-Robots.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"We often say that a recursive function &ldquo;calls itself&rdquo;.  What we "
"mean is that the instructions in a recursive function cause the Lisp "
"interpreter to run a different function that has the same name and does the "
"same job as the first, but with different arguments."
msgstr ""
"再帰関数は「自分自身を呼び出す」とよく言われます。これは、再帰関数内の命令に"
"よって、Lispインタプリタが、最初の関数と同じ名前で同じ処理を行うものの、引数"
"が異なる別の関数を実行することを意味しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Building-Robots.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"It is important that the arguments differ from one instance to the next; "
"otherwise, the process will never stop."
msgstr ""
"事例ごとに論拠が異なることが重要です。そうでなければ、プロセスが止まることは"
"ありません。"

