#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><h2>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<span>18 Conclusion<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Conclusion-1\"> &para;"
"</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>18 結論<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Conclusion-1\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"We have now reached the end of this Introduction.  You have now learned "
"enough about programming in Emacs Lisp to set values, to write simple <samp "
"class=\"file\">.emacs</samp> files for yourself and your friends, and write "
"simple customizations and extensions to Emacs."
msgstr ""
"これで本入門編の締めくくりとなります。Emacs Lispによるプログラミングについ"
"て、値の設定や、自分や友人のための簡単な<samp class=\"file\">.emacs</samp>"
"ファイルの作成、そしてEmacsの簡単なカスタマイズや拡張の作成ができるだけの知識"
"を習得できたはずです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"This is a place to stop.  Or, if you wish, you can now go onward, and teach "
"yourself."
msgstr ""
"ここは立ち寄る場所です。あるいは、よろしければ、そのまま先へ進み、独学される"
"のもよいでしょう。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You have learned some of the basic nuts and bolts of programming.  But only "
"some.  There are a great many more brackets and hinges that are easy to use "
"that we have not touched."
msgstr ""
"プログラミングの基本的な仕組みをいくつか学びました。ですが、ほんの一部に過ぎ"
"ません。まだ触れていない、使い勝手の良い括弧やヒンジが、まだまだたくさんあり"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A path you can follow right now lies among the sources to GNU Emacs and in "
"<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>."
msgstr ""
"今すぐ辿れる道筋は、GNU Emacsのソースコード群や<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU "
"Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>の中にあります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The Emacs Lisp sources are an adventure.  When you read the sources and come "
"across a function or expression that is unfamiliar, you need to figure out "
"or find out what it does."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispのソースコードを読み解くのは、まさに冒険だ。ソースを読み進めてい"
"て、見慣れない関数や式に出会ったら、それが何をするものなのかを突き止めたり、"
"調べたりする必要がある。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Go to the Reference Manual.  It is a thorough, complete, and fairly easy-to-"
"read description of Emacs Lisp.  It is written not only for experts, but for "
"people who know what you know.  (The <cite class=\"cite\">Reference Manual</"
"cite> comes with the standard GNU Emacs distribution.  Like this "
"introduction, it comes as a Texinfo source file, so you can read it on your "
"computer and as a typeset, printed book.)"
msgstr ""
"リファレンスマニュアルをご覧ください。これはEmacs Lispに関する、網羅的かつ完"
"全で、比較的読みやすい解説書です。専門家だけでなく、あなたと同等の知識を持つ"
"方に向けて書かれています。（<cite class=\"cite\">リファレンスマニュアル</"
"cite>は、標準のGNU Emacsディストリビューションに同梱されています。この入門書"
"と同様にTexinfoソースファイルとして提供されているため、コンピュータ上で閲覧で"
"きるほか、組版された印刷本としても読むことができます。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Go to the other built-in help that is part of GNU Emacs: the built-in "
"documentation for all functions and variables, and <code class=\"code\">xref-"
"find-definitions</code>, the program that takes you to sources."
msgstr ""
"GNU Emacsに組み込まれているもう一つのヘルプ、すなわちすべての関数と変数の組み"
"込みドキュメントと、ソースへ案内してくれるプログラム <code "
"class=\"code\">xref-find-definitions</code> を参照してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Here is an example of how I explore the sources.  Because of its name, <samp "
"class=\"file\">simple.el</samp> is the file I looked at first, a long time "
"ago.  As it happens some of the functions in <samp class=\"file\">simple.el</"
"samp> are complicated, or at least look complicated at first sight.  The "
"<code class=\"code\">open-line</code> function, for example, looks "
"complicated."
msgstr ""
"私がどのようにソースを調査しているか、一例を挙げます。その名の通り、<samp "
"class=\"file\">simple.el</samp>はかなり前に最初に調べたファイルです。たまたま"
"<samp class=\"file\">simple.el</samp>に含まれる関数の中には複雑なもの、あるい"
"は少なくとも一見して複雑に見えるものがあります。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">open-line</code>の関数は複雑に見えます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html
msgid ""
"You may want to walk through this function slowly, as we did with the <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> function.  (See <a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"forward_002dsentence.html\">The <code class=\"code\">forward-"
"sentence</code> function</a>.)  Or you may want to skip that function and "
"look at another, such as <code class=\"code\">split-line</code>.  You "
"don&rsquo;t need to read all the functions.  According to <code "
"class=\"code\">count-words-in-defun</code>, the <code class=\"code\">split-"
"line</code> function contains 102 words and symbols."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code>関数のときと同様に、この関数も"
"じっくりと読み進めてみるとよいでしょう。（<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"forward_002dsentence.html\"><code class=\"code\">forward-sentence</"
"code>関数</a>を参照してください。）あるいは、その関数を飛ばして、<code "
"class=\"code\">split-line</code>などの別の関数に目を向けてもよいでしょう。す"
"べての関数を読み通す必要はありません。<code class=\"code\">count-words-in-"
"defun</code>によれば、<code class=\"code\">split-line</code>関数には102個の単"
"語と記号が含まれています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Even though it is short, <code class=\"code\">split-line</code> contains "
"expressions we have not studied: <code class=\"code\">skip-chars-forward</"
"code>, <code class=\"code\">indent-to</code>, <code class=\"code\">current-"
"column</code> and <code class=\"code\">insert-and-inherit</code>."
msgstr ""
"短いながらも、<code class=\"code\">split-line</code>にはまだ学習していない式"
"<code class=\"code\">skip-chars-forward</code>、<code class=\"code\">indent-"
"to</code>、<code class=\"code\">current-column</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">insert-and-inherit</code>が含まれています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Consider the <code class=\"code\">skip-chars-forward</code> function.  In "
"GNU Emacs, you can find out more about <code class=\"code\">skip-chars-"
"forward</code> by typing <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h f</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">describe-function</code>) and the name of the function.  This "
"gives you the function documentation."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">skip-chars-forward</code> 関数を例に考えてみましょう。"
"GNU Emacs では、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h f</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">describe-function</code>) と関数名を入力することで、<code "
"class=\"code\">skip-chars-forward</code> について詳しく調べることができます。"
"これにより、関数のドキュメントが表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You may be able to guess what is done by a well named function such as <code "
"class=\"code\">indent-to</code>; or you can look it up, too.  Incidentally, "
"the <code class=\"code\">describe-function</code> function itself is in "
"<samp class=\"file\">help.el</samp>; it is one of those long, but "
"decipherable functions.  You can look up <code class=\"code\">describe-"
"function</code> using the <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h f</kbd> command!"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">indent-to</code>のような名前の付いた関数が何を行うのか、"
"推測できるかもしれません。あるいは、調べてみることもできます。ちなみに、"
"<code class=\"code\">describe-function</code>関数自体は<samp "
"class=\"file\">help.el</samp>に含まれています。これは、長いながらも解読可能な"
"関数の一つです。<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-h f</kbd>コマンドを使えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">describe-function</code>を調べることができます！"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In this instance, since the code is Lisp, the <samp class=\"file\">*Help*</"
"samp> buffer contains the name of the library containing the "
"function&rsquo;s source.  You can put point over the name of the library and "
"press the <kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd> key, which in this situation is bound "
"to <code class=\"code\">help-follow</code>, and be taken directly to the "
"source, in the same way as <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-.</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">xref-find-definitions</code>)."
msgstr ""
"この例では、コードがLispであるため、<samp class=\"file\">*Help*</samp>バッ"
"ファには関数のソースコードが含まれるライブラリ名が格納されています。ライブラ"
"リ名にポイントを置き、<kbd class=\"key\">RET</kbd>キー（この場合は<code "
"class=\"code\">help-follow</code>にバインドされています）を押すと、<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-.</kbd>（<code class=\"code\">xref-find-definitions</code>）"
"と同様に、直接ソースコードへ移動できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The definition for <code class=\"code\">describe-function</code> illustrates "
"how to customize the <code class=\"code\">interactive</code> expression "
"without using the standard character codes; and it shows how to create a "
"temporary buffer."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">describe-function</code> の定義では、標準の文字コードを"
"使わずに <code class=\"code\">interactive</code> 式をカスタマイズする方法と、"
"一時バッファを作成する方法が示されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"(The <code class=\"code\">indent-to</code> function is written in C rather "
"than Emacs Lisp; it is a built-in function.  <code class=\"code\">help-"
"follow</code> takes you to its source as does <code class=\"code\">xref-find-"
"definitions</code>, when properly set up.)"
msgstr ""
"(<code class=\"code\">indent-to</code> 関数は Emacs Lisp ではなく C で記述さ"
"れており、組み込み関数です。適切に設定されていれば、<code "
"class=\"code\">help-follow</code> や <code class=\"code\">xref-find-"
"definitions</code> でそのソースコードを参照できます。)"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You can look at a function&rsquo;s source using <code class=\"code\">xref-"
"find-definitions</code>, which is bound to <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-.</kbd> "
"Finally, you can find out what the Reference Manual has to say by visiting "
"the manual in Info, and typing <kbd class=\"kbd\">i</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">Info-index</code>) and the name of the function, or by "
"looking up the function in the index to a printed copy of the manual."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">xref-find-definitions</code> を使えば関数のソースコード"
"を参照でき、これは <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-.</kbd> にバインドされています。最後"
"に、Info でマニュアルを開き、<kbd class=\"kbd\">i</kbd> (<code "
"class=\"code\">Info-index</code>) と関数名を入力するか、あるいは印刷版マニュ"
"アルの索引で関数を調べることで、リファレンスマニュアルの記述を確認できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Similarly, you can find out what is meant by <code class=\"code\">insert-and-"
"inherit</code>."
msgstr ""
"同様に、<code class=\"code\">insert-and-inherit</code>が何を意味するのかも分"
"かります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html
msgid ""
"Other interesting source files include <samp class=\"file\">paragraphs.el</"
"samp>, <samp class=\"file\">loaddefs.el</samp>, and <samp "
"class=\"file\">loadup.el</samp>.  The <samp class=\"file\">paragraphs.el</"
"samp> file includes short, easily understood functions as well as longer "
"ones.  The <samp class=\"file\">loaddefs.el</samp> file contains the many "
"standard autoloads and many keymaps.  I have never looked at it all; only at "
"parts.  <samp class=\"file\">loadup.el</samp> is the file that loads the "
"standard parts of Emacs; it tells you a great deal about how Emacs is "
"built.  (See <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/"
"emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Building-Emacs.html#Building-Emacs\">Building "
"Emacs</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</"
"cite>, for more about building.)"
msgstr ""
"その他の興味深いソースファイルには、<samp class=\"file\">paragraphs.el</"
"samp>、<samp class=\"file\">loaddefs.el</samp>、<samp "
"class=\"file\">loadup.el</samp>などがあります。<samp "
"class=\"file\">paragraphs.el</samp>ファイルには、短くて分かりやすい関数のほ"
"か、長めの関数も含まれています。<samp class=\"file\">loaddefs.el</samp>ファイ"
"ルには、数多くの標準的なオートロードやキーマップが収録されています。私はその"
"すべてに目を通したことはなく、一部だけを見てきました。<samp "
"class=\"file\">loadup.el</samp>はEmacsの標準部分をロードするファイルであり、"
"Emacsがどのように構築されているかについて多くのことを教えてくれます。（ビルド"
"に関する詳細は、<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</"
"cite>の<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/elisp/Building-Emacs.html#Building-Emacs\">Building Emacs</"
"a>を参照してください。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"As I said, you have learned some nuts and bolts; however, and very "
"importantly, we have hardly touched major aspects of programming; I have "
"said nothing about how to sort information, except to use the predefined "
"<code class=\"code\">sort</code> function; I have said nothing about how to "
"store information, except to use variables and lists; I have said nothing "
"about how to write programs that write programs.  These are topics for "
"another, and different kind of book, a different kind of learning."
msgstr ""
"先ほど申し上げた通り、基礎的な事項をいくつか学んでいただきました。しかし、非"
"常に重要な点として、プログラミングの主要な側面にはほとんど触れていません。あ"
"らかじめ定義された<code class=\"code\">sort</code>関数を使うこと以外、情報の"
"並べ替え方については何も述べていません。変数やリストを使うこと以外、情報の保"
"存方法についても何も述べていません。そして、プログラムを書くプログラムをどう"
"書くかについても、何も述べていません。これらは別の、異なる種類の本、そして異"
"なる種類の学習で扱うべきテーマです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Conclusion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"What you have done is learn enough for much practical work with GNU Emacs.  "
"What you have done is get started.  This is the end of a beginning."
msgstr ""
"あなたは、GNU Emacsを用いた多くの実践的な作業に十分対応できる程度まで習得しま"
"した。あなたは、第一歩を踏み出したのです。これで、始まりは終わりました。"

