# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The type of data that should be passed to a function depends on what kind of "
"information it uses.  The arguments to a function such as <code "
"class=\"code\">+</code> must have values that are numbers, since <code "
"class=\"code\">+</code> adds numbers.  Other functions use different kinds "
"of data for their arguments."
msgstr ""
"関数に渡すべきデータの種類は、その関数がどのような情報を用いるかによって異な"
"ります。<code class=\"code\">+</code>のような関数の引数は、<code "
"class=\"code\">+</code>が数値を加算するため、数値である必要があります。他の関"
"数では、引数に異なる種類のデータを用います。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-concat\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-concat\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"For example, the <code class=\"code\">concat</code> function links together "
"or unites two or more strings of text to produce a string.  The arguments "
"are strings.  Concatenating the two character strings <code "
"class=\"code\">abc</code>, <code class=\"code\">def</code> produces the "
"single string <code class=\"code\">abcdef</code>.  This can be seen by "
"evaluating the following:"
msgstr ""
"例えば、<code class=\"code\">concat</code> 関数は2つ以上のテキスト文字列を連"
"結または結合して、1つの文字列を生成します。引数は文字列です。2つの文字文字列 "
"<code class=\"code\">abc</code> と <code class=\"code\">def</code> を連結する"
"と、単一の文字列 <code class=\"code\">abcdef</code> が生成されます。これは、"
"以下を評価することで確認できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(concat &quot;abc&quot; &quot;def&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The value produced by evaluating this expression is <code "
"class=\"code\">&quot;abcdef&quot;</code>."
msgstr ""
"この式を評価して得られる値は <code class=\"code\">&quot;abcdef&quot;</code> "
"です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-substring\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-substring\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A function such as <code class=\"code\">substring</code> uses both a string "
"and numbers as arguments.  The function returns a part of the string, a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">substring</em> of the first argument.  This function takes "
"three arguments.  Its first argument is the string of characters, the second "
"and third arguments are numbers that indicate the beginning (inclusive) and "
"end (exclusive) of the substring.  The numbers are a count of the number of "
"characters (including spaces and punctuation) from the beginning of the "
"string.  Note that the characters in a string are numbered from zero, not "
"one."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">substring</code> のような関数は、文字列と数値の両方を引"
"数として受け取ります。この関数は、文字列の一部、すなわち第1引数の<em "
"class=\"dfn\">部分文字列</em>を返します。この関数は3つの引数を取ります。第1引"
"数は文字の文字列であり、第2および第3引数は部分文字列の開始位置（含む）と終了"
"位置（含まない）を示す数値です。これらの数値は、文字列の先頭からの文字数（ス"
"ペースや句読点を含む）を表しています。なお、文字列内の文字は1ではなく0から番"
"号が振られている点に注意してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "For example, if you evaluate the following:"
msgstr "例えば、以下を評価する場合："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(substring &quot;The quick brown fox jumped.&quot; 16 19)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"you will see <code class=\"code\">&quot;fox&quot;</code> appear in the echo "
"area.  The arguments are the string and the two numbers."
msgstr ""
"エコーエリアに <code class=\"code\">&quot;fox&quot;</code> が表示されます。引"
"数は文字列と2つの数値です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Data-types.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Note that the string passed to <code class=\"code\">substring</code> is a "
"single atom even though it is made up of several words separated by spaces.  "
"Lisp counts everything between the two quotation marks as part of the "
"string, including the spaces.  You can think of the <code "
"class=\"code\">substring</code> function as a kind of atom smasher since it "
"takes an otherwise indivisible atom and extracts a part.  However, <code "
"class=\"code\">substring</code> is only able to extract a substring from an "
"argument that is a string, not from another type of atom such as a number or "
"symbol."
msgstr ""
"なお、<code class=\"code\">substring</code> に渡される文字列は、スペースで区"
"切られた複数の単語で構成されていても、単一のアトムであることに注意してくださ"
"い。Lisp は、スペースを含め、2つの引用符の間にあるすべてを文字列の一部として"
"カウントします。<code class=\"code\">substring</code> 関数は、本来分割不可能"
"なアトムから一部を抽出するため、いわば「アトム・スマッシャー」のようなものだ"
"と考えることができます。ただし、<code class=\"code\">substring</code> が部分"
"文字列を抽出できるのは、文字列である引数からのみであり、数値やシンボルといっ"
"た他の種類のアトムからは抽出できません。"

