# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Debugging-Exercises.html
msgid ""
"Install the <code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> function and "
"then cause it to enter the built-in debugger when you call it.  Run the "
"command on a region containing two words.  You will need to press <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">d</kbd> a remarkable number of times.  On your system, is a "
"hook called after the command finishes? (For information on hooks, see <a "
"data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/elisp/Command-Overview.html#Command-Overview\">Command Loop "
"Overview</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</"
"cite>.)"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> 関数をインストールし、呼び出"
"し時に組み込みデバッガに入るようにしてください。2つの単語を含む領域に対してこ"
"のコマンドを実行してください。<kbd class=\"kbd\">d</kbd> を驚くほど何度も押す"
"必要があります。お使いのシステムでは、コマンドの実行後にフックが呼び出されま"
"すか？（フックに関する情報については、<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs "
"Lisp Reference Manual</cite> の <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Command-"
"Overview.html#Command-Overview\">Command Loop Overview</a> を参照してくださ"
"い。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Debugging-Exercises.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Copy <code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> into the <samp "
"class=\"file\">*scratch*</samp> buffer, instrument the function for Edebug, "
"and walk through its execution.  The function does not need to have a bug, "
