# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><h4>
#: build/html/eintr/Height-of-label.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<span>What height should the label be?<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#What-height-should-the-label-be_003f\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>ラベルの高さはどのくらいにすべきですか？<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#What-height-should-the-label-be_003f\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Height-of-label.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The next issue is what height the label should be? Suppose the maximum "
"height of tallest column of the graph is seven.  Should the highest label on "
"the Y axis be &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">5 -</samp>&rsquo;, and should the "
"graph stick up above the label? Or should the highest label be &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">7 -</samp>&rsquo;, and mark the peak of the graph? Or should "
"the highest label be <code class=\"code\">10 -</code>, which is a multiple "
"of five, and be higher than the topmost value of the graph?"
msgstr ""
"次の問題は、ラベルの高さをどの程度にすべきかということです。例えば、グラフの"
"最も高い列の最大高さが7であるとします。Y軸の最高ラベルを「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">5 -</samp>」とし、グラフをラベルより上に伸ばすべきでしょうか。"
"あるいは、最高ラベルを「<samp class=\"samp\">7 -</samp>」としてグラフの頂点を"
"示すべきでしょうか。それとも、5の倍数であり、かつグラフの最大値よりも高い"
"「<code class=\"code\">10 -</code>」を最高ラベルとすべきでしょうか。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Height-of-label.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The latter form is preferred.  Most graphs are drawn within rectangles whose "
"sides are an integral number of steps long&mdash;5, 10, 15, and so on for a "
"step distance of five.  But as soon as we decide to use a step height for "
"the vertical axis, we discover that the simple expression in the varlist for "
"computing the height is wrong.  The expression is <code "
"class=\"code\">(apply 'max numbers-list)</code>.  This returns the precise "
"height, not the maximum height plus whatever is necessary to round up to the "
"nearest multiple of five.  A more complex expression is required."
msgstr ""
"後者の形式が好ましい。ほとんどのグラフは、辺の長さが整数ステップ（ステップ距"
"離が5の場合は5、10、15など）である矩形内に描画される。しかし、垂直軸にステッ"
"プ高さを用いることにした途端、高さを計算するためのvarlist内の単純な式が間違っ"
"ていることに気づく。その式は<code class=\"code\">(apply 'max numbers-list)</"
"code>である。これは正確な高さを返すのであり、最大高さに5の倍数に切り上げるた"
"めに必要な値を加算したものではない。より複雑な式が必要となる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Height-of-label.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"As usual in cases like this, a complex problem becomes simpler if it is "
"divided into several smaller problems."
msgstr ""
"こうした場合にいつもそうであるように、複雑な問題はいくつかの小さな問題に分割"
"すれば単純になる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Height-of-label.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"First, consider the case when the highest value of the graph is an integral "
"multiple of five&mdash;when it is 5, 10, 15, or some higher multiple of "
"five.  We can use this value as the Y axis height."
msgstr ""
"まず、グラフの最大値が5の整数倍である場合――すなわち5、10、15、あるいはそれ以"
"上の5の倍数である場合――を考えてみましょう。この値をY軸の高さとして用いること"
"ができます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Height-of-label.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A fairly simply way to determine whether a number is a multiple of five is "
"to divide it by five and see if the division results in a remainder.  If "
"there is no remainder, the number is a multiple of five.  Thus, seven "
"divided by five has a remainder of two, and seven is not an integral "
"multiple of five.  Put in slightly different language, more reminiscent of "
"the classroom, five goes into seven once, with a remainder of two.  However, "
"five goes into ten twice, with no remainder: ten is an integral multiple of "
"five."
msgstr ""
"ある数が5の倍数であるかどうかを判断する比較的簡単な方法は、その数を5で割り、"
"余りが出るかどうかを確認することです。余りがなければ、その数は5の倍数となりま"
"す。したがって、7を5で割ると余りが2となり、7は5の整数倍ではありません。もう少"
"し教室での説明に近い表現で言えば、5は7に1回入り、余りが2となります。一方、5は"
"10に2回入り、余りはありません。つまり、10は5の整数倍です。"

