# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/How-the-Interpreter-Acts.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-returned-value-explained\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-returned-value-explained\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/How-the-Interpreter-Acts.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"After evaluating an expression, the Lisp interpreter will most likely <em "
"class=\"dfn\">return</em> the value that the computer produces by carrying "
"out the instructions it found in the function definition, or perhaps it will "
"give up on that function and produce an error message.  (The interpreter may "
"also find itself tossed, so to speak, to a different function or it may "
"attempt to repeat continually what it is doing for ever and ever in an "
"infinite loop.  These actions are less common; and we can ignore them.)  "
"Most frequently, the interpreter returns a value."
msgstr ""
"式を評価すると、Lispインタプリタは、関数定義にある命令を実行してコンピュータ"
"が算出した値を<em class=\"dfn\">返す</em>か、あるいはその関数の処理を断念して"
"エラーメッセージを出す可能性が高いでしょう。（インタプリタは、いわば別の関数"
"へと放り出されたり、あるいは無限ループの中で現在の処理を延々と繰り返し続けよ"
"うとしたりすることもあります。こうした挙動は稀であり、無視して構いません。）"
"ほとんどの場合、インタプリタは値を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/How-the-Interpreter-Acts.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-side-effect-defined\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-side-effect-defined\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/How-the-Interpreter-Acts.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"At the same time the interpreter returns a value, it may do something else "
"as well, such as move a cursor or copy a file; this other kind of action is "
"called a <em class=\"dfn\">side effect</em>.  Actions that we humans think "
"are important, such as printing results, are often side effects to the Lisp "
"interpreter.  It is fairly easy to learn to use side effects."
msgstr ""
"インタプリタは値を返すと同時に、カーソルの移動やファイルのコピーといった別の"
"処理を行うこともあります。こうした別の種類の動作を<em class=\"dfn\">副作用</"
"em>と呼びます。結果の出力など、人間にとって重要だと思われる処理は、Lispインタ"
"プリタにおいては副作用であることが多いです。副作用の使い方を習得するのは比較"
"的簡単です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/How-the-Interpreter-Acts.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In summary, evaluating a symbolic expression most commonly causes the Lisp "
"interpreter to return a value and perhaps carry out a side effect; or else "
"produce an error."
msgstr ""
"まとめると、記号式を評価すると、多くの場合、Lispインタプリタは値を返し、場合"
"によっては副作用を発生させるか、あるいはエラーを発生させます。"

