"Consider the function <code class=\"code\">zap-to-char</code>.  Its "
"interactive expression is"
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">zap-to-char</code> を考えます。そのインタラクティブ"
"な式は"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Interactive-Options.html
#: build/html/eintr/zap_002dto_002dchar-interactive.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(interactive &quot;p\\ncZap to char: &quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Interactive-Options.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The first part of the argument to <code class=\"code\">interactive</code> is "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">p</samp>&rsquo;, with which you are already "
"familiar.  This argument tells Emacs to interpret a prefix, as a number to "
"be passed to the function.  You can specify a prefix either by typing <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-u</kbd> followed by a number or by typing <kbd "
"class=\"key\">META</kbd> followed by a number.  The prefix is the number of "
"specified characters.  Thus, if your prefix is three and the specified "
"character is &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo;, then you will "
"delete all the text up to and including the third next &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo;.  If you do not set a prefix, then you delete "
"all the text up to and including the specified character, but no more."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">interactive</code> への引数の第1部分は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">p</samp>&rsquo; であり、これについてはすでにご存知のことでしょ"
"う。この引数は、プレフィックスを関数に渡す数値として解釈するよう Emacs に指示"
"します。プレフィックスは、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-u</kbd> と入力して数値を続ける"
"か、あるいは <kbd class=\"key\">META</kbd> と入力して数値を続けることで指定で"
"きます。プレフィックスは、指定された文字数となります。したがって、プレフィッ"
"クスが 3 で、指定文字が &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo; の場合、"
"3 番目の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">x</samp>&rsquo; までのすべてのテキスト"
"（その文字自体を含む）が削除されます。プレフィックスを設定しない場合は、指定"
"された文字までのすべてのテキストが削除されますが、それ以上の範囲は削除されま"
"せん。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Interactive-Options.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">c</samp>&rsquo; tells the function the name "
"of the character to which to delete."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">c</samp>&rsquo;は、削除対象の文字名を関数に伝えま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Interactive-Options.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"More formally, a function with two or more arguments can have information "
"passed to each argument by adding parts to the string that follows <code "
"class=\"code\">interactive</code>.  When you do this, the information is "
"passed to each argument in the same order it is specified in the <code "
"class=\"code\">interactive</code> list.  In the string, each part is "
"separated from the next part by a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\n</"
"samp>&rsquo;, which is a newline.  For example, you can follow &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">p</samp>&rsquo; with a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\n</"
"samp>&rsquo; and an &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">cZap to char: </"
"samp>&rsquo;.  This causes Emacs to pass the value of the prefix argument "
"(if there is one) and the character."
msgstr ""
"より厳密に言えば、2つ以上の引数を持つ関数では、<code "
"class=\"code\">interactive</code> に続く文字列に部分を追加することで、各引数"
"に情報を渡すことができます。このようにすると、情報は <code "
"class=\"code\">interactive</code> リストで指定された順序通りに各引数に渡され"
"ます。文字列内では、各部分は改行を表す &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\n</"
"samp>&rsquo; によって区切られます。例えば、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">p</"
"samp>&rsquo; の後に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\n</samp>&rsquo; と &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">cZap to char: </samp>&rsquo; を続けることができます。こ"
"れにより、Emacs はプレフィックス引数（もしあれば）の値と文字を渡します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Interactive-Options.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In this case, the function definition looks like the following, where <code "
"class=\"code\">arg</code> and <code class=\"code\">char</code> are the "
"symbols to which <code class=\"code\">interactive</code> binds the prefix "
"argument and the specified character:"
msgstr ""
"この場合、関数定義は次のようになります。ここで <code class=\"code\">arg</"
"code> と <code class=\"code\">char</code> は、<code "
"class=\"code\">interactive</code> が接頭辞引数と指定文字を束縛するシンボルで"
"す。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Interactive-Options.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun <var class=\"var\">name-of-function</var> (arg char)\n"
"  &quot;<var class=\"var\">documentation</var>...&quot;\n"
"  (interactive &quot;p\\ncZap to char: &quot;)\n"
"  <var class=\"var\">body-of-function</var>...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Interactive-Options.html
msgid ""
"(The space after the colon in the prompt makes it look better when you are "
"prompted.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"copy_002dto_002dbuffer.html\">The "
"Definition of <code class=\"code\">copy-to-buffer</code></a>, for an "
"example.)"
msgstr ""
"（プロンプトのコロン以降のスペースを入れると、プロンプトが表示された際に見栄"
