msgid ""
"<span>Differences Between Lexical and Dynamic Binding<a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#Differences-Between-Lexical-and-Dynamic-Binding\"> &para;</"
"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>レキシカルバインディングとダイナミックバインディングの違い<a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Differences-Between-Lexical-and-Dynamic-"
"Binding\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Lexical-_0026-Dynamic-Binding-Differences.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Lexical-binding\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Binding_002c-lexical\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Lexical-binding\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Binding_002c-lexical\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lexical-_0026-Dynamic-Binding-Differences.html
msgid ""
"As we discussed before (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Prevent-"
"confusion.html\"><code class=\"code\">let</code> Prevents Confusion</a>), "
"when you create local variables with <code class=\"code\">let</code> under "
"lexical binding, those variables are valid only within the body of the <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> expression.  In other parts of your code, they "
"have other meanings, so if you call a function defined elsewhere within the "
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> body, that function would be unable to "
"&ldquo;see&rdquo; the local variables you&rsquo;ve created.  (On the other "
"hand, if you call a function that was defined within a <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> body, that function <em class=\"emph\">would</em> "
"be able to see&mdash;and modify&mdash;the local variables from that <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> expression.)"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Lexical-_0026-Dynamic-Binding-Differences.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Dynamic-binding\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Binding_002c-dynamic\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Dynamic-binding\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Binding_002c-dynamic\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lexical-_0026-Dynamic-Binding-Differences.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Under dynamic binding, the rules are different: instead, when you use <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code>, the local variables you&rsquo;ve created are "
"valid during execution of the <code class=\"code\">let</code> expression.  "
"This means that, if your <code class=\"code\">let</code> expression calls a "
"function, that function can see these local variables, regardless of where "
"the function is defined (including in another file entirely)."
msgstr ""
"動的バインディングではルールが異なります。代わりに <code class=\"code\">let</"
"code> を使用すると、作成したローカル変数は <code class=\"code\">let</code> 式"
"の実行中に有効になります。つまり、<code class=\"code\">let</code> 式が関数を"
"呼び出す場合、その関数は定義場所（完全に別のファイルであっても）に関わらず、"
"これらのローカル変数を参照できるということです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lexical-_0026-Dynamic-Binding-Differences.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Another way to think about <code class=\"code\">let</code> when using "
"dynamic binding is that every variable name has a global &ldquo;stack&rdquo; "
"of bindings, and whenever you use that variable&rsquo;s name, it refers to "
"the binding on the top of the stack.  (You can imagine this like a stack of "
"papers on your desk with the values written on them.)  When you bind a "
"variable dynamically with <code class=\"code\">let</code>, it puts the new "
"binding you&rsquo;ve specified on the top of the stack, and then executes "
"the <code class=\"code\">let</code> body.  Once the <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> body finishes, it takes that binding off of the "
"stack, revealing the one it had (if any) before the <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> expression."
msgstr ""
"動的バインディングを使用する際の <code class=\"code\">let</code> の捉え方とし"
"て、すべての変数名にはグローバルな「スタック」状のバインディングが存在し、そ"
"の変数名を使用するたびにスタックの最上部にあるバインディングが参照される、と"
"いう考え方があります。（これは、机の上に値を書き込んだ紙が積み重なっている様"
"子を想像すると分かりやすいでしょう。）<code class=\"code\">let</code> で変数"
"を動的にバインドすると、指定した新しいバインディングがスタックの最上部に追加"
"され、その後 <code class=\"code\">let</code> の本体が実行されます。<code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> の本体が終了すると、そのバインディングがスタックか"
"ら取り除かれ、<code class=\"code\">let</code> 式の前に存在していたバインディ"
"ング（もしあれば）が明らかになります。"

