# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lisp-History.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Lisp was first developed in the late 1950s at the Massachusetts Institute of "
"Technology for research in artificial intelligence.  The great power of the "
"Lisp language makes it superior for other purposes as well, such as writing "
"editor commands and integrated environments."
msgstr ""
"Lispは1950年代後半、マサチューセッツ工科大学において人工知能の研究用に初めて"
"開発されました。Lisp言語の強力な機能により、エディタコマンドや統合開発環境の"
"作成など、他の用途においても優れた性能を発揮します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Lisp-History.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Maclisp\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-Common-Lisp\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Maclisp\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-Common-Lisp\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lisp-History.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"GNU Emacs Lisp is largely inspired by Maclisp, which was written at MIT in "
"the 1960s.  It is somewhat inspired by Common Lisp, which became a standard "
"in the 1980s.  However, Emacs Lisp is much simpler than Common Lisp.  (The "
"standard Emacs distribution contains an optional extensions file, <samp "
"class=\"file\">cl-lib.el</samp>, that adds many Common Lisp features to "
"Emacs Lisp.)"
msgstr ""
"GNU Emacs Lispは、1960年代にMITで開発されたMaclispから大きな影響を受けていま"
"す。また、1980年代に標準となったCommon Lispからも一定の影響を受けています。し"
"かし、Emacs LispはCommon Lispよりもはるかにシンプルです。（標準のEmacsディス"
"トリビューションには、多くのCommon Lispの機能をEmacs Lispに追加するオプション"
"の拡張ファイル <samp class=\"file\">cl-lib.el</samp> が含まれています。）"

