"segment of computer memory called a <em class=\"dfn\">cons cell</em> "
"(because it&rsquo;s what the function <code class=\"code\">cons</code> "
"actually creates).  That cons cell also holds the address of a second cons "
"cell, whose <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> is the atom &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">violet</samp>&rsquo;; and that address (the one that tells "
"where to find &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">violet</samp>&rsquo;) is kept "
"along with the address of a third cons cell which holds the address for the "
"atom &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">buttercup</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"例えば、リスト <code class=\"code\">(rose violet buttercup)</code> には "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">rose</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">violet</samp>&rsquo;、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">buttercup</"
"samp>&rsquo; という3つの要素があります。コンピュータ内では、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">rose</samp>&rsquo; の電子アドレスは、<em class=\"dfn\">consセ"
"ル</em>と呼ばれるコンピュータメモリのセグメントに記録されています（関数 "
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code> が実際に作成するのがこれであるためです）。そ"
"のconsセルは、さらに2つ目のconsセルのアドレスも保持しており、その <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> はアトム &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">violet</"
"samp>&rsquo; となっています。そして、そのアドレス（&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">violet</samp>&rsquo; がどこにあるかを示すもの）は、アトム "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">buttercup</samp>&rsquo; のアドレスを保持する3つ目"
"のconsセルのアドレスと共に保存されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"This sounds more complicated than it is and is easier seen in a diagram:"
msgstr "これは実際よりも複雑に聞こえますし、図で見たほうがわかりやすいです："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Attribute 'alt' of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><div><img>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "cons-1"
msgstr "cons-1"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In the diagram, each box represents a word of computer memory that holds a "
"Lisp object, usually in the form of a memory address.  The boxes, i.e., the "
"addresses, are in pairs.  Each arrow points to what the address is the "
"address of, either an atom or another pair of addresses.  The first box is "
"the electronic address of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">rose</samp>&rsquo; and "
"the arrow points to &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">rose</samp>&rsquo;; the "
"second box is the address of the next pair of boxes, the first part of which "
"is the address of &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">violet</samp>&rsquo; and the "
"second part of which is the address of the next pair.  The very last box "
"points to the symbol <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, which marks the end of "
"the list."
msgstr ""
"この図において、各ボックスはLispオブジェクト（通常はメモリアドレスの形式）を"
"格納するコンピュータメモリ上のワードを表している。ボックス、すなわちアドレス"
"はペアになっている。各矢印は、そのアドレスが指す先、すなわちアトムか、あるい"
"は別のアドレスペアのいずれかを示している。最初のボックスは&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">rose</samp>&rsquo;の電子アドレスであり、矢印は&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">rose</samp>&rsquo;を指している。2番目のボックスは次のボックス"
"ペアのアドレスであり、その前半部分は&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">violet</"
"samp>&rsquo;のアドレス、後半部分は次のペアのアドレスとなっている。一番最後の"
"ボックスはシンボル<code class=\"code\">nil</code>を指しており、これがリストの"
"終端を示している。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When a variable is set to a list with an operation such as <code "
"class=\"code\">setq</code>, it stores the address of the first box in the "
"variable.  Thus, evaluation of the expression"
msgstr ""
"変数に <code class=\"code\">setq</code> のような演算を用いてリストを代入する"
"と、変数には最初のボックスのアドレスが格納されます。したがって、式の評価は"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq bouquet '(rose violet buttercup))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "creates a situation like this:"
msgstr "次のような状況になります："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Attribute 'alt' of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><div><img>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "cons-2"
msgstr "cons-2"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In this example, the symbol <code class=\"code\">bouquet</code> holds the "
"address of the first pair of boxes."
msgstr ""
"この例では、記号 <code class=\"code\">bouquet</code> が最初の一組のボックスの"
"アドレスを保持しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"This same list can be illustrated in a different sort of box notation like "
"this:"
msgstr "同じリストを、次のような別の形式のボックス表記で示すこともできます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Attribute 'alt' of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><div><img>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "cons-2a"
msgstr "cons-2a"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"(Symbols consist of more than pairs of addresses, but the structure of a "
"symbol is made up of addresses.  Indeed, the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">bouquet</code> consists of a group of address-boxes, one of "
"which is the address of the printed word &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">bouquet</samp>&rsquo;, a second of which is the address of a "
"function definition attached to the symbol, if any, a third of which is the "
"address of the first pair of address-boxes for the list <code "
"class=\"code\">(rose violet buttercup)</code>, and so on.  Here we are "
"showing that the symbol&rsquo;s third address-box points to the first pair "
"of address-boxes for the list.)"
msgstr ""
"（シンボルはアドレスのペア以上の要素から構成されるが、シンボルの構造はアドレ"
"スによって成り立っている。実際、シンボル <code class=\"code\">bouquet</code> "
"はアドレスボックスの集合から成り、その一つは印刷語 &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">bouquet</samp>&rsquo; のアドレスであり、二つ目は（もしあれば）"
"シンボルに付随する関数定義のアドレスであり、三つ目はリスト <code "
"class=\"code\">(rose violet buttercup)</code> の最初のアドレスボックスのペア"
"のアドレスであり、以下同様である。ここでは、シンボルの三番目のアドレスボック"
"スが、リストの最初のアドレスボックスのペアを指していることを示している。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If a symbol is set to the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of a list, the "
"list itself is not changed; the symbol simply has an address further down "
"the list.  (In the jargon, <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> and <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> are &ldquo;non-destructive&rdquo;.)  Thus, "
"evaluation of the following expression"
msgstr ""
"シンボルがリストの<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>に設定されている場合、リスト"
"自体は変更されず、単にそのシンボルがリストのより後方のアドレスを持つことにな"
"ります。（専門用語では、<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>と<small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small>は「非破壊的」と呼ばれます。）したがって、以下の式の"
"評価は"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq flowers (cdr bouquet))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/eintr/Sorting.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "produces this:"
msgstr "以下を生成します："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Attribute 'alt' of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><div><img>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "cons-3"
msgstr "cons-3"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The value of <code class=\"code\">flowers</code> is <code "
"class=\"code\">(violet buttercup)</code>, which is to say, the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">flowers</code> holds the address of the pair of address-"
"boxes, the first of which holds the address of <code class=\"code\">violet</"
"code>, and the second of which holds the address of <code "
"class=\"code\">buttercup</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">flowers</code>の値は<code class=\"code\">(violet "
"buttercup)</code>であり、すなわち、記号<code class=\"code\">flowers</code>は"
"アドレスボックスのペアのアドレスを保持しており、その1つ目は<code "
"class=\"code\">violet</code>のアドレスを、2つ目は<code "
"class=\"code\">buttercup</code>のアドレスを保持している。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dotted-pair\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-cons-cell\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-dotted-pair\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-cons-cell\"></a>"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html
msgid ""
"A pair of address-boxes is called a <em class=\"dfn\">cons cell</em> or <em "
"class=\"dfn\">dotted pair</em>.  See <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Cons-Cell-Type.html#Cons-"
"Cell-Type\">Cons Cell and List Types</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU "
"Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>, and <a data-manual=\"elisp\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Dotted-Pair-"
"Notation.html#Dotted-Pair-Notation\">Dotted Pair Notation</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>, for more "
"information about cons cells and dotted pairs."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">cons</code> adds a new pair of addresses "
"to the front of a series of addresses like that shown above.  For example, "
"evaluating the expression"
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">cons</code> は、上記に示すような一連のアドレスの先"
"頭に、新たなアドレスのペアを追加します。例えば、次の式を評価すると、"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq bouquet (cons 'lily bouquet))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Attribute 'alt' of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><div><img>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "cons-4"
msgstr "cons-4"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"However, this does not change the value of the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">flowers</code>, as you can see by evaluating the following,"
msgstr ""
"しかし、これはシンボル <code class=\"code\">flowers</code> の値を変えるもので"
"はなく、以下を評価すればわかる通り、"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(eq (cdr (cdr bouquet)) flowers)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "which returns <code class=\"code\">t</code> for true."
msgstr "true の場合に <code class=\"code\">t</code> を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Until it is reset, <code class=\"code\">flowers</code> still has the value "
"<code class=\"code\">(violet buttercup)</code>; that is, it has the address "
"of the cons cell whose first address is of <code class=\"code\">violet</"
"code>.  Also, this does not alter any of the pre-existing cons cells; they "
"are all still there."
msgstr ""
"リセットされるまで、<code class=\"code\">flowers</code>は依然として値<code "
"class=\"code\">(violet buttercup)</code>を保持している。つまり、第1アドレスが"
"<code class=\"code\">violet</code>であるコンスセルのアドレスを保持しているこ"
"とになる。また、これにより既存のコンスセルが変更されることはなく、すべてその"
"まま存在し続ける。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Thus, in Lisp, to get the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of a list, you "
"just get the address of the next cons cell in the series; to get the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of a list, you get the address of the first element "
"of the list; to <code class=\"code\">cons</code> a new element on a list, "
"you add a new cons cell to the front of the list.  That is all there is to "
"it! The underlying structure of Lisp is brilliantly simple!"
msgstr ""
"このように、Lispでリストの<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>を取得するには、単に"
"系列内の次のコンスセルのアドレスを取得すればよい。リストの<small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small>を取得するには、リストの最初の要素のアドレスを取得す"
"ればよい。リストに新しい要素を<code class=\"code\">cons</code>追加するには、"
"リストの先頭に新しいコンスセルを追加すればよい。たったこれだけだ！Lispの根底"
"にある構造は、見事にシンプルだ！"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"And what does the last address in a series of cons cells refer to? It is the "
"address of the empty list, of <code class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"では、一連のconsセルにおける最後のアドレスは何を指すのでしょうか？それは空リ"
"スト、すなわち<code class=\"code\">nil</code>のアドレスです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Lists-diagrammed.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In summary, when a Lisp variable is set to a value, it is provided with the "
"address of the list to which the variable refers."
msgstr ""
"まとめると、Lispの変数に値が代入される際、その変数が参照するリストのアドレス"
"が併せて提供されます。"

