# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Loops-_0026-Recursion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Emacs Lisp has two primary ways to cause an expression, or a series of "
"expressions, to be evaluated repeatedly: one uses a <code "
"class=\"code\">while</code> loop, and the other uses <em "
"class=\"dfn\">recursion</em>."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispには、式または一連の式を繰り返し評価させるための主要な方法が2つあり"
"ます。一つは<code class=\"code\">while</code>ループを用いる方法で、もう一つは"
"<em class=\"dfn\">再帰</em>を用いる方法です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Loops-_0026-Recursion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Repetition can be very valuable.  For example, to move forward four "
"sentences, you need only write a program that will move forward one sentence "
"and then repeat the process four times.  Since a computer does not get bored "
"or tired, such repetitive action does not have the deleterious effects that "
"excessive or the wrong kinds of repetition can have on humans."
msgstr ""
"反復は非常に有用な場合があります。例えば、4文分先に進むには、1文分進み、その"
"処理を4回繰り返すというプログラムを書くだけで済みます。コンピュータは飽きたり"
"疲れたりすることがないため、こうした反復的な動作は、過度あるいは不適切な種類"
"の反復が人間に及ぼし得るような悪影響をもたらすことはありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Loops-_0026-Recursion.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"People mostly write Emacs Lisp functions using <code class=\"code\">while</"
"code> loops and their kin; but you can use recursion, which provides a very "
"powerful way to think about and then to solve problems<a class=\"footnote\" "
"id=\"DOCF14\" href=\"#FOOT14\"><sup>14</sup></a>."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispの関数は、主に<code class=\"code\">while</code>ループやその類を用い"
"て記述されますが、再帰を使うこともできます。再帰は、問題を考え、そして解決す"
"るための非常に強力な手法となります<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF14\" "
"href=\"#FOOT14\"><sup>14</sup></a>。"

