# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><h3>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<span>1.3 Generate an Error Message<a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Generate-an-Error-Message\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>1.3 エラーメッセージの生成<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Generate-"
"an-Error-Message\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Generate-an-error-message\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Error-message-generation\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Generate-an-error-message\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Error-message-generation\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Partly so you won&rsquo;t worry if you do it accidentally, we will now give "
"a command to the Lisp interpreter that generates an error message.  This is "
"a harmless activity; and indeed, we will often try to generate error "
"messages intentionally.  Once you understand the jargon, error messages can "
"be informative.  Instead of being called &ldquo;error&rdquo; messages, they "
"should be called &ldquo;help&rdquo; messages.  They are like signposts to a "
"traveler in a strange country; deciphering them can be hard, but once "
"understood, they can point the way."
msgstr ""
"一つには、うっかり実行してしまっても心配しなくて済むようにするためです。これ"
"から、エラーメッセージを生成するコマンドをLispインタプリタに発行します。これ"
"は無害な操作であり、実際、意図的にエラーメッセージを生成しようとすることもよ"
"くあります。専門用語を理解すれば、エラーメッセージは有益な情報となり得ます。"
"「エラー」メッセージと呼ぶのではなく、「ヘルプ」メッセージと呼ぶべきでしょ"
"う。それらは見知らぬ国を旅する者にとっての道標のようなものです。解読するのは"
"難しいかもしれませんが、一度理解すれば、進むべき方向を示してくれます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The error message is generated by a built-in GNU Emacs debugger.  We will "
"enter the debugger.  You get out of the debugger by typing <code "
"class=\"code\">q</code>."
msgstr ""
"このエラーメッセージは、GNU Emacs内蔵のデバッガによって生成されています。デ"
"バッガに入ります。<code class=\"code\">q</code> と入力するとデバッガを終了で"
"きます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"What we will do is evaluate a list that is not quoted and does not have a "
"meaningful command as its first element.  Here is a list almost exactly the "
"same as the one we just used, but without the single-quote in front of it.  "
"Position the cursor right after it and type <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd>:"
msgstr ""
"ここでは、クォートで囲まれておらず、かつ先頭要素に意味のあるコマンドが含まれ"
"ていないリストを評価します。以下は、先ほど使用したものとほぼ同一ですが、先頭"
"のシングルクォートがないリストです。リストの直後にカーソルを置き、<kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd> と入力してください："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(this is an unquoted list)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A <samp class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp> window will open up and you should "
"see the following in it:"
msgstr ""
"<samp class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp> ウィンドウが開き、その中に以下が表示"
"されるはずです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"---------- Buffer: *Backtrace* ----------\n"
"Debugger entered--Lisp error: (void-function this)\n"
"  (this is an unquoted list)\n"
"  (progn (this is an unquoted list))\n"
"  eval((progn (this is an unquoted list)) t)\n"
"  elisp--eval-last-sexp(nil)\n"
"  #f(compiled-function () #&lt;bytecode ...&gt;)()\n"
"  handler-bind-1(#f(compiled-function () #&lt;bytecode ...&gt;) (error) eval-expression--debug)\n"
"  eval-last-sexp(nil)\n"
"  funcall-interactively(eval-last-sexp nil)\n"
"  call-interactively(eval-last-sexp nil nil)\n"
"  command-execute(eval-last-sexp)\n"
"---------- Buffer: *Backtrace* ----------\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Your cursor will be in this window (you may have to wait a few seconds "
"before it becomes visible).  To quit the debugger and make the debugger "
"window go away, type:"
msgstr ""
"カーソルはこのウィンドウ内に表示されます（表示されるまで数秒かかる場合があり"
"ます）。デバッガを終了してデバッガウィンドウを閉じるには、以下を入力してくだ"
"さい："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "q\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Please type <kbd class=\"kbd\">q</kbd> right now, so you become confident "
"that you can get out of the debugger.  Then, type <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-"
"e</kbd> again to re-enter it."
msgstr ""
"デバッガから抜け出せるという自信が持てるよう、今すぐ <kbd class=\"kbd\">q</"
"kbd> と入力してください。その後、再度入るために <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</"
"kbd> と入力してください。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-defined\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-defined\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "Based on what we already know, we can almost read this error message."
msgstr "既知の情報からすれば、このエラーメッセージはほぼ読み取れます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You read the <samp class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp> buffer from the bottom "
"up; it tells you what Emacs did.  When you typed <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</"
"kbd>, you made an interactive call to the command <code class=\"code\">eval-"
"last-sexp</code>.  <code class=\"code\">eval</code> is an abbreviation for "
"&ldquo;evaluate&rdquo; and <code class=\"code\">sexp</code> is an "
"abbreviation for &ldquo;symbolic expression&rdquo;.  The command means "
"&ldquo;evaluate last symbolic expression&rdquo;, which is the expression "
"just before your cursor."
msgstr ""
"<samp class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp> バッファを下から上に向かって読み進め"
"ると、Emacs がどのような処理を行ったかが分かります。<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-"
"e</kbd> と入力した際、コマンド <code class=\"code\">eval-last-sexp</code> を"
"インタラクティブに呼び出しました。<code class=\"code\">eval</code> は"
"「evaluate」の略であり、<code class=\"code\">sexp</code> は「symbolic "
"expression」の略です。このコマンドは「最後のシンボリック式を評価する」という"
"意味で、カーソルの直前にある式を指します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Each line above tells you what the Lisp interpreter evaluated next.  The "
"most recent action is at the top.  The buffer is called the <samp "
"class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp> buffer because it enables you to track "
"Emacs backwards."
msgstr ""
"上記の各行は、Lispインタプリタが次に何を評価したかを示しています。直近の処理"
"が一番上に表示されます。このバッファは、Emacsを遡って追跡できるため、<samp "
"class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp>バッファと呼ばれています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"At the top of the <samp class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp> buffer, you see "
"the line:"
msgstr ""
"<samp class=\"file\">*Backtrace*</samp>バッファの先頭に、次の行があります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "Debugger entered--Lisp error: (void-function this)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The Lisp interpreter tried to evaluate the first atom of the list, the word "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">this</samp>&rsquo;.  It is this action that "
"generated the error message &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">void-function this</"
"samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"Lispインタプリタは、リストの最初のアトムである単語 &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">this</samp>&rsquo; を評価しようとしました。この動作によって、"
"エラーメッセージ &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">void-function this</"
"samp>&rsquo; が生成されました。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The message contains the words &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">void-function</"
"samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">this</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"メッセージには「<samp class=\"samp\">void-function</samp>」と「<samp "
"class=\"samp\">this</samp>」という単語が含まれています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-defined-1\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-function-defined-1\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The word &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">function</samp>&rsquo; was mentioned "
"once before.  It is a very important word.  For our purposes, we can define "
"it by saying that a <em class=\"dfn\">function</em> is a set of instructions "
"to the computer that tell the computer to do something."
msgstr ""
"「<samp class=\"samp\">function</samp>」という単語は、以前に一度登場しまし"
"た。これは非常に重要な単語です。ここでの目的においては、<em class=\"dfn\">関"
"数</em>とは、コンピュータに何らかの動作を指示する一連の命令であると定義できま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Now we can begin to understand the error message: &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">void-function this</samp>&rsquo;.  The function (that is, the "
"word &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">this</samp>&rsquo;) does not have a "
"definition of any set of instructions for the computer to carry out."
msgstr ""
"これで、エラーメッセージ「<samp class=\"samp\">void-function this</samp>」の"
"意味が分かり始めてきました。この関数（つまり「<samp class=\"samp\">this</"
"samp>」という単語）には、コンピュータが実行すべき命令セットの定義が存在しない"
"のです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The slightly odd word, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">void-function</"
"samp>&rsquo;, is designed to cover the way Emacs Lisp is implemented, which "
"is that when a symbol does not have a function definition attached to it, "
"the place that should contain the instructions is void."
msgstr ""
"少々奇妙な単語である &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">void-function</samp>&rsquo; "
"は、Emacs Lisp の実装方式、すなわちシンボルに関数定義が紐付けられていない場"
"合、命令が格納されるべき場所が空になるという仕組みをカバーするために設計され"
"ています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"On the other hand, since we were able to add 2 plus 2 successfully, by "
"evaluating <code class=\"code\">(+ 2 2)</code>, we can infer that the symbol "
"<code class=\"code\">+</code> must have a set of instructions for the "
"computer to obey and those instructions must be to add the numbers that "
"follow the <code class=\"code\">+</code>."
msgstr ""
"一方で、2 + 2 の計算を正常に行えたため、<code class=\"code\">(+ 2 2)</code> "
"を評価することで、記号 <code class=\"code\">+</code> にはコンピュータが従うべ"
"き一連の命令が存在し、それらの命令は <code class=\"code\">+</code> に続く数値"
"を加算するものでなければならないと推論できる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"It is possible to prevent Emacs entering the debugger in cases like this.  "
"We do not explain how to do that here, but we will mention what the result "
"looks like, because you may encounter a similar situation if there is a bug "
"in some Emacs code that you are using.  In such cases, you will see only one "
"line of error message; it will appear in the echo area and look like this:"
msgstr ""
"このような場合に、Emacsがデバッガに入るのを防ぐことが可能です。ここではその方"
"法を解説しませんが、使用しているEmacsのコードにバグがある場合に同様の状況に遭"
"遇する可能性があるため、その結果がどのようなものになるかについて触れておきま"
"す。そのような場合、エラーメッセージは1行だけ表示され、エコーエリアに次のよう"
"に現れます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "Symbol's function definition is void: this\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The message goes away as soon as you type a key, even just to move the "
"cursor."
msgstr ""
"キーを一つ押すだけで、たとえカーソルを動かすだけであっても、メッセージは消え"
"てしまいます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"We know the meaning of the word &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Symbol</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  It refers to the first atom of the list, the word &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">this</samp>&rsquo;.  The word &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">function</samp>&rsquo; refers to the instructions that tell "
"the computer what to do.  (Technically, the symbol tells the computer where "
"to find the instructions, but this is a complication we can ignore for the "
"moment.)"
msgstr ""
"「<samp class=\"samp\">Symbol</samp>」という単語の意味は分かっています。これ"
"はリストの最初のアトム、つまり「<samp class=\"samp\">this</samp>」という単語"
"を指します。「<samp class=\"samp\">function</samp>」という単語は、コンピュー"
"タに何をすべきかを指示する命令を指します。（厳密に言えば、この記号はコン"
"ピュータに命令がどこにあるかを伝えるものですが、この点はひとまず無視して構い"
"ません。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Making-Errors.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The error message can be understood: &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">Symbol's "
"function definition is void: this</samp>&rsquo;.  The symbol (that is, the "
"word &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">this</samp>&rsquo;) lacks instructions for "
"the computer to carry out."
msgstr ""
"エラーメッセージは次のように解釈できます：&lsquo;<samp "
