"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Parts-of-let-expression\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-varlist-defined\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Parts-of-let-Expression.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A <code class=\"code\">let</code> expression is a list of three parts.  The "
"first part is the symbol <code class=\"code\">let</code>.  The second part "
"is a list, called a <em class=\"dfn\">varlist</em>, each element of which is "
"either a symbol by itself or a two-element list, the first element of which "
"is a symbol.  The third part of the <code class=\"code\">let</code> "
"expression is the body of the <code class=\"code\">let</code>.  The body "
"usually consists of one or more lists."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> 式は3つの部分からなるリストです。第1部分はシ"
"ンボル <code class=\"code\">let</code> です。第2部分は <em "
"class=\"dfn\">varlist</em> と呼ばれるリストで、その各要素は単独のシンボルか、"
"あるいは第1要素がシンボルである2要素のリストのいずれかです。<code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> 式の第3部分は <code class=\"code\">let</code> のボ"
"ディです。ボディは通常、1つ以上のリストで構成されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Parts-of-let-Expression.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A template for a <code class=\"code\">let</code> expression looks like this:"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">let</code> 式のテンプレートは次のようになります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Parts-of-let-Expression.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(let <var class=\"var\">varlist</var> <var class=\"var\">body</var>...)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Parts-of-let-Expression.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The symbols in the varlist are the variables that are given initial values "
"by the <code class=\"code\">let</code> special form.  Symbols by themselves "
"are given the initial value of <code class=\"code\">nil</code>; and each "
"symbol that is the first element of a two-element list is bound to the value "
"that is returned when the Lisp interpreter evaluates the second element."
msgstr ""
"varlist 内のシンボルは、特殊形式 <code class=\"code\">let</code> によって初期"
"値が付与される変数である。シンボル単体には <code class=\"code\">nil</code> の"
"初期値が付与され、2要素リストの第1要素である各シンボルは、Lispインタプリタが"
"第2要素を評価した際に返される値に束縛される。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Parts-of-let-Expression.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Thus, a varlist might look like this: <code class=\"code\">(thread (needles "
"3))</code>.  In this case, in a <code class=\"code\">let</code> expression, "
"Emacs binds the symbol <code class=\"code\">thread</code> to an initial "
"value of <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, and binds the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">needles</code> to an initial value of 3."
msgstr ""
"したがって、varlistは <code class=\"code\">(thread (needles 3))</code> のよう"
"になります。この場合、<code class=\"code\">let</code> という式において、Emacs"
"はシンボル <code class=\"code\">thread</code> を初期値 <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code> に、シンボル <code class=\"code\">needles</code> を"
"初期値 3 にそれぞれバインドします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Parts-of-let-Expression.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When you write a <code class=\"code\">let</code> expression, what you do is "
"put the appropriate expressions in the slots of the <code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> expression template."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> 式を記述する際は、<code class=\"code\">let</"
"code> 式テンプレートのスロットに適切な式を代入することになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Parts-of-let-Expression.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If the varlist is composed of two-element lists, as is often the case, the "
"template for the <code class=\"code\">let</code> expression looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"varlistが2要素のリストで構成されている場合（多くの場合そうなります）、<code "
"class=\"code\">let</code>式のテンプレートは次のようになります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Parts-of-let-Expression.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(let ((<var class=\"var\">variable</var> <var class=\"var\">value</var>)\n"
"      (<var class=\"var\">variable</var> <var class=\"var\">value</var>)\n"
"      ...)\n"
"  <var class=\"var\">body</var>...)\n"
msgstr ""

