# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Readying-a-Graph.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Our goal is to construct a graph showing the numbers of function definitions "
"of various lengths in the Emacs lisp sources."
msgstr ""
"我々の目的は、EmacsのLispソースにおける、さまざまな長さの関数定義数を示すグラ"
"フを作成することです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Readying-a-Graph.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"As a practical matter, if you were creating a graph, you would probably use "
"a program such as <code class=\"code\">gnuplot</code> to do the job.  (<code "
"class=\"code\">gnuplot</code> is nicely integrated into GNU Emacs.)  In this "
"case, however, we create one from scratch, and in the process we will re-"
"acquaint ourselves with some of what we learned before and learn more."
msgstr ""
"実用面で言えば、グラフを作成するのであれば、おそらく<code "
"class=\"code\">gnuplot</code>のようなプログラムを使うことになるでしょう。"
"（<code class=\"code\">gnuplot</code>はGNU Emacsに見事に統合されています。）"
"しかし今回は、ゼロからグラフを作成します。その過程で、以前に学んだことの一部"
"を改めて復習し、さらに新たな知識を習得することになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Readying-a-Graph.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In this chapter, we will first write a simple graph printing function.  This "
"first definition will be a <em class=\"dfn\">prototype</em>, a rapidly "
"written function that enables us to reconnoiter this unknown graph-making "
"territory.  We will discover dragons, or find that they are myth.  After "
"scouting the terrain, we will feel more confident and enhance the function "
"to label the axes automatically."
msgstr ""
"本章では、まずシンプルなグラフ描画関数を作成します。最初の定義は<em "
"class=\"dfn\">プロトタイプ</em>、つまりこの未知のグラフ作成領域を偵察するため"
"に手早く書き上げた関数となります。そこでドラゴンを発見するか、あるいはそれが"
"単なる神話に過ぎないことが分かるでしょう。地形を偵察した後は、より自信がつ"
"き、軸に自動的にラベルを付けるように関数を改良していきます。"

