# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Regexp-Search.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Regular expression searches are used extensively in GNU Emacs.  The two "
"functions, <code class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code>, illustrate these searches well.  "
"They use regular expressions to find where to move point.  The phrase "
"&ldquo;regular expression&rdquo; is often written as &ldquo;regexp&rdquo;."
msgstr ""
"GNU Emacsでは、正規表現による検索が幅広く利用されています。<code "
"class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> と <code class=\"code\">forward-"
"paragraph</code> という2つの関数は、こうした検索の好例です。これらの関数は正"
"規表現を用いて、ポイントを移動させる位置を特定します。「正規表現」というフ"
"レーズは、しばしば「regexp」と表記されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Regexp-Search.html
msgid ""
"Regular expression searches are described in <a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Regexp-"
"Search.html#Regexp-Search\">Regular Expression Search</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>, as well as in <a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"elisp/Regular-Expressions.html#Regular-Expressions\">Regular Expressions</a> "
"in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>.  In "
"writing this chapter, I am presuming that you have at least a mild "
"acquaintance with them.  The major point to remember is that regular "
"expressions permit you to search for patterns as well as for literal strings "
"of characters.  For example, the code in <code class=\"code\">forward-"
"sentence</code> searches for the pattern of possible characters that could "
"mark the end of a sentence, and moves point to that spot."
msgstr ""
"正規表現による検索については、<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</"
"cite>の<a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/emacs/Regexp-Search.html#Regexp-Search\">Regular Expression "
"Search</a>、および<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</"
"cite>の<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/elisp/Regular-Expressions.html#Regular-"
"Expressions\">Regular Expressions</a>で解説されています。本章を執筆するにあた"
"り、読者の皆様がこれらについて少なくともある程度の知識をお持ちであることを前"
"提としています。特に留意すべき点は、正規表現を用いることで、リテラルな文字列"
"だけでなく、パターンの検索も可能になるということです。例えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> のコードは、文末を示す可能性のある文字"
"のパターンを検索し、ポイントをその位置に移動させます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Regexp-Search.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Before looking at the code for the <code class=\"code\">forward-sentence</"
"code> function, it is worth considering what the pattern that marks the end "
"of a sentence must be.  The pattern is discussed in the next section; "
"following that is a description of the regular expression search function, "
"<code class=\"code\">re-search-forward</code>.  The <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> function is described in the section "
"following.  Finally, the <code class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code> "
"function is described in the last section of this chapter.  <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code> is a complex function that "
"introduces several new features."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> 関数のコードを見る前に、文の終わ"
"りを示すパターンがどのようなものであるべきかを考えておく価値があります。その"
"パターンについては次の節で説明し、続いて正規表現検索関数 <code "
