# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Run-a-program\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-Program_002c-running-one\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-evaluate-defined\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Run-a-program\"></a> <a class=\"index-"
"entry-id\" id=\"index-Program_002c-running-one\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-evaluate-defined\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A list in Lisp&mdash;any list&mdash;is a program ready to run.  If you run "
"it (for which the Lisp jargon is <em class=\"dfn\">evaluate</em>), the "
"computer will do one of three things: do nothing except return to you the "
"list itself; send you an error message; or, treat the first symbol in the "
"list as a command to do something.  (Usually, of course, it is the last of "
"these three things that you really want!)"
msgstr ""
"Lispにおけるリスト――いかなるリストであっても――は、実行可能なプログラムであ"
"る。それを実行すれば（Lispの専門用語ではこれを<em class=\"dfn\">評価</em>と呼"
"ぶ）、コンピュータは次の3つのうちいずれかの動作をとる。リストそのものを返す以"
"外に何もしないか、エラーメッセージを送るか、あるいはリストの先頭のシンボルを"
"何らかの操作を行うためのコマンドとして扱うかである。（もちろん、通常本当に望"
"むのは、これら3つのうち最後のケースである！）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-quote\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-_0027-for-quoting\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-quoting-using-apostrophe\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-apostrophe-for-quoting\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-quote\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-"
"id\" id=\"index-_0027-for-quoting\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-quoting-using-apostrophe\"></a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" "
"id=\"index-apostrophe-for-quoting\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The single apostrophe, <code class=\"code\">'</code>, that I put in front of "
"some of the example lists in preceding sections is called a <em "
"class=\"dfn\">quote</em>; when it precedes a list, it tells Lisp to do "
"nothing with the list, other than take it as it is written.  But if there is "
"no quote preceding a list, the first item of the list is special: it is a "
"command for the computer to obey.  (In Lisp, these commands are called <em "
"class=\"emph\">functions</em>.)  The list <code class=\"code\">(+ 2 2)</"
"code> shown above did not have a quote in front of it, so Lisp understands "
"that the <code class=\"code\">+</code> is an instruction to do something "
"with the rest of the list: add the numbers that follow."
msgstr ""
"前節のいくつかの例示リストの前に付けた単一のアポストロフィ <code "
"class=\"code\">'</code> は、<em class=\"dfn\">クォート</em> と呼ばれます。こ"
"れがリストの前にある場合、Lisp に対してリストをそのまま受け取る以外、何も行わ"
"ないよう指示します。しかし、リストの前にクォートがない場合、リストの最初の項"
"目は特別な意味を持ちます。それは、コンピュータが従うべき命令となります。"
"（Lisp では、これらの命令を <em class=\"emph\">関数</em> と呼びます。）上に示"
"したリスト <code class=\"code\">(+ 2 2)</code> の前にはクォートがなかったた"
"め、Lisp は <code class=\"code\">+</code> がリストの残りの部分に対して何らか"
"の操作（後続の数値を加算すること）を行うよう指示していると解釈します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If you are reading this inside of GNU Emacs in Info, here is how you can "
"evaluate such a list: place your cursor immediately after the right hand "
"parenthesis of the following list and then type <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</"
"kbd>:"
msgstr ""
"GNU EmacsのInfoでこれを読んでいる場合は、次のようなリストを評価する方法があり"
"ます。以下のリストの右括弧の直後にカーソルを置き、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-"
"e</kbd>と入力してください："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You will see the number <code class=\"code\">4</code> appear in the echo "
"area<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF2\" href=\"#FOOT2\"><sup>2</sup></a>.  "
"(What you have just done is evaluate the list.  The echo area is the line at "
"the bottom of the screen that displays or echoes text.)  Now try the same "
"thing with a quoted list: place the cursor right after the following list "
"and type <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd>:"
msgstr ""
"エコー領域<a class=\"footnote\" id=\"DOCF2\" href=\"#FOOT2\"><sup>2</sup></a>"
"に数値 <code class=\"code\">4</code> が表示されます。（今行ったのはリストの評"
"価です。エコー領域とは、テキストを表示またはエコーする画面下部の行のことで"
"す。）では、引用符で囲まれたリストでも同様に試してみましょう。以下のリストの"
"直後にカーソルを置き、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd> と入力してください："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "'(this is a quoted list)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You will see <code class=\"code\">(this is a quoted list)</code> appear in "
"the echo area."
msgstr ""
"エコーエリアに <code class=\"code\">(this is a quoted list)</code> が表示され"
"ます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Lisp-interpreter_002c-explained\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Interpreter_002c-Lisp_002c-"
"explained\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Lisp-interpreter_002c-explained\"></"
"a> <a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Interpreter_002c-Lisp_002c-"
"explained\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In both cases, what you are doing is giving a command to the program inside "
"of GNU Emacs called the <em class=\"dfn\">Lisp interpreter</em>&mdash;giving "
"the interpreter a command to evaluate the expression.  The name of the Lisp "
"interpreter comes from the word for the task done by a human who comes up "
"with the meaning of an expression&mdash;who interprets it."
msgstr ""
"いずれの場合も、行っているのはGNU Emacs内部の<em class=\"dfn\">Lispインタプリ"
"タ</em>と呼ばれるプログラムへの命令――つまり、式を評価するようにインタプリタに"
"指示を出すことです。Lispインタプリタという名称は、式の意味を考え出し、それを"
"解釈する人間が行う作業を指す言葉に由来しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Run-a-Program.html
msgid ""
"You can also evaluate an atom that is not part of a list&mdash;one that is "
"not surrounded by parentheses; again, the Lisp interpreter translates from "
"the humanly readable expression to the language of the computer.  But before "
"discussing this (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"Variables.html\">Variables</"
"a>), we will discuss what the Lisp interpreter does when you make an error."
msgstr ""
"また、リストに含まれないアトム――つまり括弧で囲まれていないアトム――を評価する"
"こともできます。ここでも、Lispインタプリタは人間が読みやすい式をコンピュータ"
"の言語へと変換します。ただ、この点について説明する前に（<a class=\"pxref\" "
"href=\"Variables.html\">変数</a>を参照）、エラーが発生した際にLispインタプリ"
"タがどのような処理を行うかについて解説します。"

