# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><h3>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<span>Storing Text in a List<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Storing-Text-"
"in-a-List\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>リストにテキストを格納する<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Storing-"
"Text-in-a-List\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When text is cut out of a buffer, it is stored on a list.  Successive pieces "
"of text are stored on the list successively, so the list might look like "
"this:"
msgstr ""
"バッファからテキストが切り出されると、リストに格納されます。連続するテキスト"
"は順次リストに格納されるため、リストは次のようになる場合があります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(&quot;a piece of text&quot; &quot;previous piece&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The function <code class=\"code\">cons</code> can be used to create a new "
"list from a piece of text (an &ldquo;atom&rdquo;, to use the jargon) and an "
"existing list, like this:"
msgstr ""
"関数 <code class=\"code\">cons</code> を使うと、テキスト（専門用語でいう「ア"
"トム」）と既存のリストから、次のように新しいリストを作成できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(cons &quot;another piece&quot;\n"
"      '(&quot;a piece of text&quot; &quot;previous piece&quot;))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If you evaluate this expression, a list of three elements will appear in the "
"echo area:"
msgstr ""
"この式を評価すると、エコー領域に3つの要素からなるリストが表示されます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(&quot;another piece&quot; &quot;a piece of text&quot; &quot;previous piece&quot;)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"With the <code class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">nthcdr</"
"code> functions, you can retrieve whichever piece of text you want.  For "
"example, in the following code, <code class=\"code\">nthcdr 1 &hellip;</"
"code> returns the list with the first item removed; and the <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> returns the first element of that "
"remainder&mdash;the second element of the original list:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">car</code> と <code class=\"code\">nthcdr</code> 関数を"
"使えば、任意のテキストを取得できます。例えば、以下のコードでは、<code "
"class=\"code\">nthcdr 1 &hellip;</code> は最初の項目を除いたリストを返し、"
"<code class=\"code\">car</code> はその残りのリストの最初の要素――つまり元のリ"
"ストの2番目の要素――を返します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(car (nthcdr 1 '(&quot;another piece&quot;\n"
"                 &quot;a piece of text&quot;\n"
"                 &quot;previous piece&quot;)))\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;a piece of text&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The actual functions in Emacs are more complex than this, of course.  The "
"code for cutting and retrieving text has to be written so that Emacs can "
"figure out which element in the list you want&mdash;the first, second, "
"third, or whatever.  In addition, when you get to the end of the list, Emacs "
"should give you the first element of the list, rather than nothing at all."
msgstr ""
"もちろん、Emacsの実際の機能はこれよりも複雑です。テキストの切り取りや取得を行"
"うコードは、リストのどの要素（1番目、2番目、3番目など）を意図しているのかを"
"Emacsが判別できるように記述する必要があります。さらに、リストの末尾に達した"
"際、Emacsは何も返さず、リストの最初の要素を返すべきです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The list that holds the pieces of text is called the <em class=\"dfn\">kill "
"ring</em>.  This chapter leads up to a description of the kill ring and how "
"it is used by first tracing how the <code class=\"code\">zap-to-char</code> "
"function works.  This function calls a function that invokes a function that "
"manipulates the kill ring.  Thus, before reaching the mountains, we climb "
"the foothills."
msgstr ""
"テキストの断片を保持するリストは、<em class=\"dfn\">キルリング</em>と呼ばれま"
"す。本章では、まず<code class=\"code\">zap-to-char</code>関数の仕組みを辿るこ"
"とで、キルリングの説明とその利用方法へとつなげていきます。この関数は、キルリ"
"ングを操作する関数を呼び出す関数を、さらに呼び出すという構造になっています。"
"つまり、山に到達する前に、まずは山麓を登るというわけです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Storing-Text.html
msgid ""
"A subsequent chapter describes how text that is cut from the buffer is "
"retrieved.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Yanking.html\">Yanking Text Back</"
"a>."
msgstr ""
"続く章では、バッファから切り出されたテキストをどのように復元するかについて説"
"明します。<a class=\"xref\" href=\"Yanking.html\">テキストのヤンク</a>を参照"
"してください。"

