msgstr ""
"<span>1.10 まとめ<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Summary-1\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Learning Lisp is like climbing a hill in which the first part is the "
"steepest.  You have now climbed the most difficult part; what remains "
"becomes easier as you progress onwards."
msgstr ""
"Lispを学ぶことは、最初の方が最も急な丘を登るようなものです。今は最も困難な部"
"分を登り終えました。この先へ進むにつれ、残りの道のりは楽になっていきます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "In summary,"
msgstr "まとめると、"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Lisp programs are made up of expressions, which are lists or single atoms."
msgstr "Lispプログラムは、リストまたは単一のアトムである式で構成されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Lists are made up of zero or more atoms or inner lists, separated by "
"whitespace and surrounded by parentheses.  A list can be empty."
msgstr ""
"リストは、0個以上のアトムまたは内部リストで構成され、空白文字で区切られ、括弧"
"で囲まれます。リストは空であっても構いません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Atoms are multi-character symbols, like <code class=\"code\">forward-"
"paragraph</code>, single character symbols like <code class=\"code\">+</"
"code>, strings of characters between double quotation marks, or numbers."
msgstr ""
"アトムは、<code class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code>のような複数文字の記"
"号、<code class=\"code\">+</code>のような単一文字の記号、ダブルクォートで囲ま"
"れた文字列、あるいは数値です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "A number evaluates to itself."
msgstr "ある数は、それ自身と等しくなる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "A string between double quotes also evaluates to itself."
msgstr "ダブルクォートで囲まれた文字列も、それ自体として評価されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "When you evaluate a symbol by itself, its value is returned."
msgstr "シンボル単体を評価すると、その値が返されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When you evaluate a list, the Lisp interpreter looks at the first symbol in "
"the list and then at the function definition bound to that symbol.  Then the "
"instructions in the function definition are carried out."
msgstr ""
"リストを評価する際、Lispインタプリタはリストの先頭のシンボルを参照し、次にそ"
"のシンボルに束縛された関数定義を参照します。その後、関数定義内の命令が実行さ"
"れます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A single-quote &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo; tells the Lisp "
"interpreter that it should return the following expression as written, and "
"not evaluate it as it would if the quote were not there."
msgstr ""
"シングルクォート &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">'</samp>&rsquo; は、Lispインタプ"
"リタに対し、後続の式をクォートがない場合のように評価するのではなく、記述され"
"た通りに返すよう指示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Arguments are the information passed to a function.  The arguments to a "
"function are computed by evaluating the rest of the elements of the list of "
"which the function is the first element."
msgstr ""
"引数とは、関数に渡される情報のことです。関数の引数は、その関数を先頭要素とす"
"るリストの残りの要素を評価することで算出されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/Summary.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A function always returns a value when it is evaluated (unless it gets an "
"error); in addition, it may also carry out some action that is a side "
"effect.  In many cases, a function&rsquo;s primary purpose is to create a "
"side effect."
msgstr ""
"関数は評価される際、常に値を返します（エラーが発生した場合を除く）。さらに、"
"副作用となる何らかの処理を行うこともあります。多くの場合、関数の主な目的は副"
"作用を生み出すことにあります。"

