# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html
msgid ""
"Emacs treats different characters as belonging to different <em "
"class=\"dfn\">syntax categories</em>.  For example, the regular expression, "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\w+</samp>&rsquo;, is a pattern specifying "
"one or more <em class=\"emph\">word constituent</em> characters.  Word "
"constituent characters are members of one syntax category.  Other syntax "
"categories include the class of punctuation characters, such as the period "
"and the comma, and the class of whitespace characters, such as the blank "
"space and the tab character.  (For more information, see <a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"elisp/Syntax-Tables.html#Syntax-Tables\">Syntax Tables</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>.)"
msgstr ""
"Emacsでは、異なる文字をそれぞれ異なる<em class=\"dfn\">構文カテゴリ</em>に属"
"するものとして扱います。例えば、正規表現 &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\w+</"
"samp>&rsquo; は、1つ以上の<em class=\"emph\">単語構成文字</em>を指定するパ"
"ターンです。単語構成文字は、ある一つの構文カテゴリに属します。その他の構文カ"
"テゴリには、ピリオドやカンマなどの句読点文字のクラスや、空白やタブ文字などの"
"空白文字のクラスがあります。（詳細については、<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU "
"Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Syntax-Tables.html#Syntax-"
"Tables\">構文テーブル</a>を参照してください。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Syntax tables specify which characters belong to which categories.  Usually, "
"a hyphen is not specified as a word constituent character.  Instead, it is "
"specified as being in the class of characters that are part of symbol names "
"but not words.  This means that the <code class=\"code\">count-words-"
"example</code> function treats it in the same way it treats an interword "
"white space, which is why <code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> "
"counts &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">multiply-by-seven</samp>&rsquo; as three "
"words."
msgstr ""
"構文表では、どの文字がどのカテゴリに属するかが規定されています。通常、ハイフ"
"ンは単語構成文字としては指定されません。その代わりに、記号名の一部ではあるが"
"単語ではない文字のクラスに属するものとして指定されます。つまり、<code "
"class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> 関数はこれを単語間の空白と同様に扱"
"うため、<code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">multiply-by-seven</samp>&rsquo; を3つの単語としてカウントしま"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"There are two ways to cause Emacs to count &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">multiply-by-seven</samp>&rsquo; as one symbol: modify the "
"syntax table or modify the regular expression."
msgstr ""
"Emacsに&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">multiply-by-seven</samp>&rsquo;を1つのシン"
"ボルとしてカウントさせるには、構文テーブルを変更するか、正規表現を変更するか"
"の2通りの方法があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"We could redefine a hyphen as a word constituent character by modifying the "
"syntax table that Emacs keeps for each mode.  This action would serve our "
"purpose, except that a hyphen is merely the most common character within "
"symbols that is not typically a word constituent character; there are "
"others, too."
msgstr ""
"Emacsがモードごとに保持している構文テーブルを修正することで、ハイフンを単語構"
"成文字として再定義することも可能です。この方法でも目的は達成できますが、ハイ"
"フンは単に記号の中で最も頻出する文字に過ぎず、通常は単語構成文字ではありませ"
"ん。他にも該当する文字は存在します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Alternatively, we can redefine the regexp used in the <code "
"class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> definition so as to include "
"symbols.  This procedure has the merit of clarity, but the task is a little "
"tricky."
msgstr ""
"あるいは、<code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> の定義で使用する正"
"規表現を、記号を含めるように再定義することもできます。この手法は明快であると"
"いう利点がありますが、作業は少し手間がかかります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The first part is simple enough: the pattern must match at least one "
"character that is a word or symbol constituent.  Thus:"
msgstr ""
"前半部分はいたってシンプルです。パターンは、単語または記号の構成要素である文"
"字のうち、少なくとも1文字に一致しなければなりません。したがって："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "&quot;\\\\(\\\\w\\\\|\\\\s_\\\\)+&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\(</samp>&rsquo; is the first part of the "
"grouping construct that includes the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\w</"
"samp>&rsquo; and the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\s_</samp>&rsquo; as "
"alternatives, separated by the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\|</"
"samp>&rsquo;.  The &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\w</samp>&rsquo; matches "
"any word-constituent character and the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\s_</"
"samp>&rsquo; matches any character that is part of a symbol name but not a "
"word-constituent character.  The &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo; "
"following the group indicates that the word or symbol constituent characters "
"must be matched at least once."
msgstr ""
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\(</samp>&rsquo;は、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\\\w</samp>&rsquo;と&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\s_</"
"samp>&rsquo;を代替候補として含み、それらを&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\|</"
"samp>&rsquo;で区切ったグループ化構文の第1部分です。&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\\\w</samp>&rsquo;は任意の単語構成文字にマッチし、&lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\s_</samp>&rsquo;は記号名の一部でありながら単語構成文"
"字ではない任意の文字にマッチします。グループに続く&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">+</samp>&rsquo;は、単語または記号の構成文字が少なくとも1回は"
"マッチしなければならないことを示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"However, the second part of the regexp is more difficult to design.  What we "
"want is to follow the first part with optionally one or more characters that "
"are not constituents of a word or symbol.  At first, I thought I could "
"define this with the following:"
msgstr ""
"しかし、正規表現の後半部分の設計はより困難です。実現したいのは、前半部分に続"
"いて、単語や記号の構成要素ではない文字を任意に1文字以上配置することです。当初"
"は、次のように定義できると考えていました。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "&quot;\\\\(\\\\W\\\\|\\\\S_\\\\)*&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The upper case &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">W</samp>&rsquo; and &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">S</samp>&rsquo; match characters that are <em "
"class=\"emph\">not</em> word or symbol constituents.  Unfortunately, this "
"expression matches any character that is either not a word constituent or "
"not a symbol constituent.  This matches any character!"
msgstr ""
"大文字の &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">W</samp>&rsquo; と &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">S</samp>&rsquo; は、単語や記号の構成要素<em class=\"emph\">で"
"はない</em>文字にマッチします。残念ながら、この式は単語の構成要素でも記号の構"
"成要素でもないあらゆる文字にマッチしてしまいます。つまり、どんな文字にもマッ"
"チしてしまうのです！"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"I then noticed that every word or symbol in my test region was followed by "
"white space (blank space, tab, or newline).  So I tried placing a pattern to "
"match one or more blank spaces after the pattern for one or more word or "
"symbol constituents.  This failed, too.  Words and symbols are often "
"separated by whitespace, but in actual code parentheses may follow symbols "
"and punctuation may follow words.  So finally, I designed a pattern in which "
"the word or symbol constituents are followed optionally by characters that "
"are not white space and then followed optionally by white space."
msgstr ""
"そこで、テスト領域内のすべての単語や記号の後に、空白（スペース、タブ、または"
"改行）が続いていることに気づきました。そこで、1つ以上の単語や記号の構成要素の"
"パターンの後に、1つ以上の空白にマッチするパターンを配置してみました。しかし、"
"これもうまくいきませんでした。単語や記号は多くの場合空白で区切られています"
"が、実際のコードでは、記号の後に括弧が続いたり、単語の後に句読点が続いたりす"
"ることがあります。そこで最終的に、単語や記号の構成要素の後に、任意で空白以外"
"の文字が続き、さらにその後に任意で空白が続くというパターンを設計しました。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "Here is the full regular expression:"
msgstr "正規表現の全文は以下の通りです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Syntax.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "&quot;\\\\(\\\\w\\\\|\\\\s_\\\\)+[^ \\t\\n]*[ \\t\\n]*&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

