# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Truth-_0026-Falsehood.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"There is an important aspect to the truth test in an <code "
"class=\"code\">if</code> expression.  So far, we have spoken of "
"&ldquo;true&rdquo; and &ldquo;false&rdquo; as values of predicates as if "
"they were new kinds of Emacs Lisp objects.  In fact, &ldquo;false&rdquo; is "
"just our old friend <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  Anything "
"else&mdash;anything at all&mdash;is &ldquo;true&rdquo;."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">if</code> 式における真理値判定には、重要な側面がありま"
"す。これまで、「真」と「偽」を、あたかも新しい種類の Emacs Lisp オブジェクト"
"であるかのように、述語の値として扱ってきました。実際には、「偽」とは単にお馴"
"染みの <code class=\"code\">nil</code> にすぎません。それ以外のもの――文字通り"
"あらゆるもの――が「真」となるのです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Truth-_0026-Falsehood.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The expression that tests for truth is interpreted as <em "
"class=\"dfn\">true</em> if the result of evaluating it is a value that is "
"not <code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  In other words, the result of the test "
"is considered true if the value returned is a number such as 47, a string "
"such as <code class=\"code\">&quot;hello&quot;</code>, or a symbol (other "
"than <code class=\"code\">nil</code>) such as <code class=\"code\">flowers</"
"code>, or a list (so long as it is not empty), or even a buffer!"
msgstr ""
"真偽を判定する式は、評価結果が<code class=\"code\">nil</code>以外の値である場"
"合に<em class=\"dfn\">真</em>と解釈されます。言い換えれば、返される値が47のよ"
"うな数値、<code class=\"code\">&quot;hello&quot;</code>のような文字列、<code "
"class=\"code\">flowers</code>のようなシンボル（<code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>を除く）、リスト（空でない限り）、あるいはバッファであってもよいというこ"
"とです！"

