msgid ""
"<span>3.6.3 Uninitialized Variables in a <code class=\"code\">let</code> "
"Statement<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Uninitialized-Variables-in-a-let-"
"Statement\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>3.6.3 <code class=\"code\">let</code> 文における未初期化変数<a "
"class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Uninitialized-Variables-in-a-let-"
"Statement\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Uninitialized-let-Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Uninitialized-let-variables\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-let-variables-uninitialized\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Uninitialized-let-variables\"></a> <a "
"class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-let-variables-uninitialized\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Uninitialized-let-Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If you do not bind the variables in a <code class=\"code\">let</code> "
"statement to specific initial values, they will automatically be bound to an "
"initial value of <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, as in the following "
"expression:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> 文で変数を特定の初期値にバインドしない場合、"
"以下の式のように、それらは自動的に <code class=\"code\">nil</code> の初期値に"
"バインドされます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Uninitialized-let-Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(let ((birch 3)\n"
"      pine\n"
"      fir\n"
"      (oak 'some))\n"
"  (message\n"
"   &quot;Here are %d variables with %s, %s, and %s value.&quot;\n"
"   birch pine fir oak))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Uninitialized-let-Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Here, the varlist is <code class=\"code\">((birch 3) pine fir (oak 'some))</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"ここで、varlistは<code class=\"code\">((birch 3) pine fir (oak 'some))</code>"
"です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Uninitialized-let-Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If you evaluate this expression in the usual way, the following will appear "
"in your echo area:"
msgstr "この式を通常の方法で評価すると、エコー領域に以下のように表示されます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Uninitialized-let-Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "&quot;Here are 3 variables with nil, nil, and some value.&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Uninitialized-let-Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In this example, Emacs binds the symbol <code class=\"code\">birch</code> to "
"the number 3, binds the symbols <code class=\"code\">pine</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">fir</code> to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, and binds the "
"symbol <code class=\"code\">oak</code> to the value <code "
"class=\"code\">some</code>."
msgstr ""
"この例では、Emacsはシンボル <code class=\"code\">birch</code> を数値 3 に、シ"
"ンボル <code class=\"code\">pine</code> と <code class=\"code\">fir</code> "
"を <code class=\"code\">nil</code> に、そしてシンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">oak</code> を値 <code class=\"code\">some</code> にそれぞれバ"
"インドします。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Uninitialized-let-Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Note that in the first part of the <code class=\"code\">let</code>, the "
"variables <code class=\"code\">pine</code> and <code class=\"code\">fir</"
"code> stand alone as atoms that are not surrounded by parentheses; this is "
"because they are being bound to <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, the empty "
"list.  But <code class=\"code\">oak</code> is bound to <code "
"class=\"code\">some</code> and so is a part of the list <code "
"class=\"code\">(oak 'some)</code>.  Similarly, <code class=\"code\">birch</"
"code> is bound to the number 3 and so is in a list with that number.  (Since "
"a number evaluates to itself, the number does not need to be quoted.  Also, "
"the number is printed in the message using a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%d</"
"samp>&rsquo; rather than a &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%s</samp>&rsquo;.)  "
"The four variables as a group are put into a list to delimit them from the "
"body of the <code class=\"code\">let</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> の前半部分において、変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">pine</code> と <code class=\"code\">fir</code> は括弧で囲まれ"
"ないアトムとして単独で存在している点に注意してください。これは、これらが空リ"
"ストである <code class=\"code\">nil</code> に束縛されているためです。一方、"
"<code class=\"code\">oak</code> は <code class=\"code\">some</code> に束縛さ"
"れており、リスト <code class=\"code\">(oak 'some)</code> の一部となっていま"
"す。同様に、<code class=\"code\">birch</code> は数値 3 に束縛されており、その"
"数値を含むリストの中に存在しています。（数値はそれ自体として評価されるため、"
"クォートする必要はありません。また、メッセージ内では数値は &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">%s</samp>&rsquo; ではなく &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">%d</"
"samp>&rsquo; として出力されます。）これら4つの変数はまとめてリストに入れら"
"れ、<code class=\"code\">let</code> の本体から区切られています。"

