#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><h4>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<span>1.9.1 Using <code class=\"code\">setq</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Using-setq-1\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>1.9.1 <code class=\"code\">setq</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#Using-setq-1\"> &para;</a> の使用</span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-set\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-set\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"To set the value of the symbol <code class=\"code\">flowers</code> to the "
"list <code class=\"code\">(rose violet daisy buttercup)</code>, evaluate the "
"following expression by positioning the cursor after the expression and "
"typing <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"記号 <code class=\"code\">flowers</code> の値をリスト <code "
"class=\"code\">(rose violet daisy buttercup)</code> に設定するには、式の後に"
"カーソルを置き、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd> と入力して次の式を評価してく"
"ださい。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq flowers '(rose violet daisy buttercup))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The list <code class=\"code\">(rose violet daisy buttercup)</code> will "
"appear in the echo area.  This is what is <em class=\"emph\">returned</em> "
"by the <code class=\"code\">setq</code> special form.  As a side effect, the "
"symbol <code class=\"code\">flowers</code> is bound to the list; that is, "
"the symbol <code class=\"code\">flowers</code>, which can be viewed as a "
"variable, is given the list as its value.  (This process, by the way, "
"illustrates how a side effect to the Lisp interpreter, setting the value, "
"can be the primary effect that we humans are interested in.  This is because "
"every Lisp function must return a value if it does not get an error, but it "
"will only have a side effect if it is designed to have one.)"
msgstr ""
"リスト <code class=\"code\">(rose violet daisy buttercup)</code> がエコーエリ"
"アに表示されます。これが <code class=\"code\">setq</code> 特殊形式によって"
"<em class=\"emph\">返される</em>ものです。副次的な効果として、シンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">flowers</code> がリストに束縛されます。つまり、変数と見なせる"
"シンボル <code class=\"code\">flowers</code> に、その値としてリストが代入され"
"るということです。（ちなみに、このプロセスは、値を設定するという Lisp インタ"
"プリタへの副次的な効果が、我々人間が関心を寄せる主たる効果となり得ることを示"
"しています。というのも、すべての Lisp 関数は、エラーが発生しなければ値を返さ"
"なければなりませんが、副次的な効果を持つように設計されていない限り、副次的な"
"効果のみを持つことになるからです。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"After evaluating the <code class=\"code\">setq</code> expression, you can "
"evaluate the symbol <code class=\"code\">flowers</code> and it will return "
"the value you just set.  Here is the symbol.  Place your cursor after it and "
"type <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">setq</code> 式を評価した後、シンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">flowers</code> を評価すると、先ほど設定した値が返されます。こ"
"ちらがそのシンボルです。シンボルの後にカーソルを置き、<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x "
"C-e</kbd> と入力してください。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "flowers\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When you evaluate <code class=\"code\">flowers</code>, the list <code "
"class=\"code\">(rose violet daisy buttercup)</code> appears in the echo area."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">flowers</code>を評価すると、エコー領域にリスト<code "
"class=\"code\">(rose violet daisy buttercup)</code>が表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Incidentally, if you evaluate <code class=\"code\">'flowers</code>, the "
"variable with a quote in front of it, what you will see in the echo area is "
"the symbol itself, <code class=\"code\">flowers</code>.  Here is the quoted "
"symbol, so you can try this:"
msgstr ""
"ちなみに、前にクォートが付いた変数 <code class=\"code\">'flowers</code> を評"
"価すると、エコー領域に表示されるのはシンボルそのものである <code "
"class=\"code\">flowers</code> です。こちらがクォート付きのシンボルですので、"
"ぜひお試しください："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "'flowers\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Also, as an added convenience, <code class=\"code\">setq</code> permits you "
"to set several different variables to different values, all in one "
"expression."
msgstr ""
"また、さらなる利便性として、<code class=\"code\">setq</code> では一つの式の中"
"で、複数の異なる変数にそれぞれ異なる値を設定できます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"To set the value of the variable <code class=\"code\">carnivores</code> to "
"the list <code class=\"code\">'(lion tiger leopard)</code> using <code "
"class=\"code\">setq</code>, the following expression is used:"
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\">carnivores</code> の値を <code "
"class=\"code\">setq</code> を用いてリスト <code class=\"code\">'(lion tiger "
"leopard)</code> に設定するには、次の式を使用します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(setq carnivores '(lion tiger leopard))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Also, <code class=\"code\">setq</code> can be used to assign different "
"values to different variables.  The first argument is bound to the value of "
"the second argument, the third argument is bound to the value of the fourth "
"argument, and so on.  For example, you could use the following to assign a "
"list of trees to the symbol <code class=\"code\">trees</code> and a list of "
"herbivores to the symbol <code class=\"code\">herbivores</code>:"
msgstr ""
"また、<code class=\"code\">setq</code> を使用して、異なる変数に異なる値を代入"
"することもできます。第1引数は第2引数の値に、第3引数は第4引数の値に、というよ"
"うにそれぞれ紐付けられます。例えば、以下のようにして、樹木のリストをシンボル "
"<code class=\"code\">trees</code> に、草食動物のリストをシンボル <code "
"class=\"code\">herbivores</code> に代入できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(setq trees '(pine fir oak maple)\n"
"      herbivores '(gazelle antelope zebra))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"(The expression could just as well have been on one line, but it might not "
"have fit on a page; and humans find it easier to read nicely formatted "
"lists.)"
msgstr ""
"（この表現は1行でもよかったかもしれませんが、ページに収まりきらなかったかもし"
"れません。また、人間はきれいに整形されたリストの方が読みやすいと感じるもので"
"す。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Using-setq.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Although I have been using the term &ldquo;assign&rdquo;, there is another "
"way of thinking about the workings of <code class=\"code\">setq</code>; and "
"that is to say that <code class=\"code\">setq</code> makes the symbol <em "
"class=\"emph\">point</em> to the list.  This latter way of thinking is very "
"common and in forthcoming chapters we shall come upon at least one symbol "
"that has &ldquo;pointer&rdquo; as part of its name.  The name is chosen "
"because the symbol has a value, specifically a list, attached to it; or, "
"expressed another way, the symbol is set to point to the list."
msgstr ""
"これまで「代入」という用語を用いてきましたが、<code class=\"code\">setq</"
"code>の仕組みには別の考え方もあります。それは、<code class=\"code\">setq</"
"code>がシンボルをリストへと<em class=\"emph\">指し示す</em>というものです。後"
"者の考え方は非常に一般的であり、今後の章では、名称の一部に「ポインタ」を含む"
"シンボルに少なくとも一つは出会うことになります。この名称が選ばれたのは、その"
"シンボルに値、具体的にはリストが紐付いているためです。言い換えれば、そのシン"
"ボルはリストを指すように設定されているということです。"

