"a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>1.7 変数<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#Variables-1\"> &para;</a></"
"span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Variables\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Variables\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In Emacs Lisp, a symbol can have a value attached to it just as it can have "
"a function definition attached to it.  The two are different.  The function "
"definition is a set of instructions that a computer will obey.  A value, on "
"the other hand, is something, such as number or a name, that can vary (which "
"is why such a symbol is called a variable).  The value of a symbol can be "
"any expression in Lisp, such as a symbol, number, list, or string.  A symbol "
"that has a value is often called a <em class=\"dfn\">variable</em>."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispでは、シンボルには関数定義が紐付けられるのと同様に、値を紐付けるこ"
"ともできます。この2つは異なります。関数定義とは、コンピュータが実行する一連の"
"命令のことです。一方、値とは、数値や名前のように変動しうるもののことです（そ"
"のため、このようなシンボルは変数と呼ばれます）。シンボルの値は、シンボル、数"
"値、リスト、文字列など、Lispにおけるあらゆる式になり得ます。値を持つシンボル"
"は、しばしば<em class=\"dfn\">変数</em>と呼ばれます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"A symbol can have both a function definition and a value attached to it at "
"the same time.  Or it can have just one or the other.  The two are "
"separate.  This is somewhat similar to the way the name Cambridge can refer "
"to the city in Massachusetts and have some information attached to the name "
"as well, such as &ldquo;great programming center&rdquo;."
msgstr ""
"シンボルには、関数定義と値の両方を同時に持たせることができます。あるいは、ど"
"ちらか一方のみを持たせることも可能です。この2つは別物です。これは、「ケンブ"
"リッジ」という名称がマサチューセッツ州の都市を指すと同時に、「優れたプログラ"
"ミングセンター」といった情報も付随しているのと、ある意味で似ています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Variables.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Another way to think about this is to imagine a symbol as being a chest of "
"drawers.  The function definition is put in one drawer, the value in "
"another, and so on.  What is put in the drawer holding the value can be "
"changed without affecting the contents of the drawer holding the function "
"definition, and vice versa."
msgstr ""
"別の考え方として、シンボルを引き出し箱に見立ててみる方法があります。関数定義"
"を一つの引き出しに、値を別の引き出しに、というように入れていきます。値が入っ"
"ている引き出しの中身は、関数定義が入っている引き出しの中身に影響を与えること"
"なく変更でき、その逆も同様です。"

