# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><h3>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<span>For Whom This is Written<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#For-Whom-"
"This-is-Written\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>誰のために書かれたか<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#For-Whom-This-"
"is-Written\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"This text is written as an elementary introduction for people who are not "
"programmers.  If you are a programmer, you may not be satisfied with this "
"primer.  The reason is that you may have become expert at reading reference "
"manuals and be put off by the way this text is organized."
msgstr ""
"本書は、プログラマーではない方向けの入門書として執筆されています。プログラ"
"マーの方にとっては、この入門書では物足りなく感じられるかもしれません。という"
"のも、リファレンスマニュアルを読みこなすことに習熟しており、本書の構成に違和"
"感を覚える可能性があるからです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "An expert programmer who reviewed this text said to me:"
msgstr "この文章を校閲した熟練のプログラマーが、私にこう言った。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><blockquote><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<i class=\"i\">I prefer to learn from reference manuals.  I &ldquo;dive "
"into&rdquo; each paragraph, and &ldquo;come up for air&rdquo; between "
"paragraphs.</i>"
msgstr ""
"<i class=\"i\">私はリファレンスマニュアルから学ぶ方が好きです。各段落に「飛び"
"込み」、段落の合間に「息継ぎ」をします。</i>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><blockquote><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<i class=\"i\">When I get to the end of a paragraph, I assume that subject "
"is done, finished, that I know everything I need (with the possible "
"exception of the case when the next paragraph starts talking about it in "
"more detail).  I expect that a well written reference manual will not have a "
"lot of redundancy, and that it will have excellent pointers to the (one) "
"place where the information I want is.</i>"
msgstr ""
"<i class=\"i\">段落の最後まで読み進めると、その主題についてはこれで終わり、完"
"結し、必要な情報はすべて揃ったのだと考えます（次の段落でより詳しく触れられる"
"場合は別ですが）。よく書かれたリファレンスマニュアルであれば、冗長な記述は少"
"なく、欲しい情報が載っている（唯一の）場所への的確な案内があるだろうと期待し"
"ています。</i>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "This introduction is not written for this person!"
msgstr "この紹介文は、この人向けに書かれていない！"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Firstly, I try to say everything at least three times: first, to introduce "
"it; second, to show it in context; and third, to show it in a different "
"context, or to review it."
msgstr ""
"まず、あらゆることを少なくとも3回は伝えるようにしています。1回目は紹介するた"
"め、2回目は文脈の中で示すため、そして3回目は別の文脈で示すか、あるいは復習す"
"るためです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Secondly, I hardly ever put all the information about a subject in one "
"place, much less in one paragraph.  To my way of thinking, that imposes too "
"heavy a burden on the reader.  Instead I try to explain only what you need "
"to know at the time.  (Sometimes I include a little extra information so you "
"won&rsquo;t be surprised later when the additional information is formally "
"introduced.)"
msgstr ""
"次に、ある主題に関するすべての情報を一箇所にまとめることはほとんどありません"
"し、ましてや一つの段落に収めることなどまずありません。私の考えでは、それでは"
"読者に過度な負担を強いることになるからです。その代わりに、その時点で知ってお"
"くべきことだけを説明するようにしています。（時折、少し補足情報を盛り込むこと"
"もあります。そうすることで、後でその情報が正式に導入された際に、読者が驚かず"
"に済むからです。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When you read this text, you are not expected to learn everything the first "
"time.  Frequently, you need make only a nodding acquaintance with some of "
"the items mentioned.  My hope is that I have structured the text and given "
"you enough hints that you will be alert to what is important, and "
"concentrate on it."
msgstr ""
"この文章を読む際、一度ですべてを習得できるとは限りません。多くの場合、挙げら"
"れている項目のいくつかに、軽く目を通すだけで十分でしょう。私がこの文章を構成"
"し、十分なヒントを提示したことで、何が重要であるかに気づき、そこに集中してい"
"ただけることを願っています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You will need to dive into some paragraphs; there is no other way to read "
"them.  But I have tried to keep down the number of such paragraphs.  This "
"book is intended as an approachable hill, rather than as a daunting mountain."
msgstr ""
"いくつかの段落はじっくり読み込む必要があります。そうする以外に読み方はありま"
"せん。ただ、そうした段落の数は極力抑えるよう努めました。本書は、そびえ立つ山"
"ではなく、親しみやすい丘となることを意図しています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Who-You-Are.html
msgid ""
"This book, <cite class=\"cite\">An Introduction to Programming in Emacs "
"Lisp</cite>, has a companion document, <a data-manual=\"elisp\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/"
"index.html#Top\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>.  The reference "
"manual has more detail than this introduction.  In the reference manual, all "
"the information about one topic is concentrated in one place.  You should "
"turn to it if you are like the programmer quoted above.  And, of course, "
"after you have read this <cite class=\"cite\">Introduction</cite>, you will "
"find the <cite class=\"cite\">Reference Manual</cite> useful when you are "
"writing your own programs."
msgstr ""
"本書『<cite class=\"cite\">An Introduction to Programming in Emacs Lisp</"
"cite>』には、『<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</"
"cite>』という関連ドキュメント、<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/index.html#Top\">The GNU "
"Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</a>があります。リファレンスマニュアルは、本入門書"
"よりも詳細な内容となっています。リファレンスマニュアルでは、あるトピックに関"
"するすべての情報が一箇所にまとめられています。前述のプログラマーのような方"
"は、ぜひそちらを参照してください。そしてもちろん、この『<cite "
