msgid ""
"<span>14.1 What to Count?<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#What-to-"
"Count_003f\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>14.1 何をカウントするか？<a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#What-to-"
"Count_003f\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/Words-and-Symbols.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Words-and-symbols-in-defun\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-Words-and-symbols-in-defun\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Words-and-Symbols.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When we first start thinking about how to count the words in a function "
"definition, the first question is (or ought to be) what are we going to "
"count? When we speak of &ldquo;words&rdquo; with respect to a Lisp function "
"definition, we are actually speaking, in large part, of symbols.  For "
"example, the following <code class=\"code\">multiply-by-seven</code> "
"function contains the five symbols <code class=\"code\">defun</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">multiply-by-seven</code>, <code class=\"code\">number</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">*</code>, and <code class=\"code\">7</code>.  In "
"addition, in the documentation string, it contains the four words &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">Multiply</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">NUMBER</samp>&rsquo;, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">by</"
"samp>&rsquo;, and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">seven</samp>&rsquo;.  The "
"symbol &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">number</samp>&rsquo; is repeated, so the "
"definition contains a total of ten words and symbols."
msgstr ""
"関数定義における「単語」をどう数えるかを考え始める際、まず問われるのは（ある"
"いは問われるべきなのは）、一体何を数えるのかということです。Lispの関数定義に"
"関して「単語」と言うとき、実際にはその大部分はシンボルのことを指しています。"
"例えば、以下の <code class=\"code\">multiply-by-seven</code> 関数には、<code "
"class=\"code\">defun</code>、<code class=\"code\">multiply-by-seven</code>、"
"<code class=\"code\">number</code>、<code class=\"code\">*</code>、<code "
"class=\"code\">7</code> という5つのシンボルが含まれています。さらに、ドキュメ"
"ント文字列には、<samp class=\"samp\">Multiply</samp>、<samp "
"class=\"samp\">NUMBER</samp>、<samp class=\"samp\">by</samp>、<samp "
"class=\"samp\">seven</samp> という4つの単語が含まれています。シンボル <samp "
"class=\"samp\">number</samp> は重複して出現しているため、この定義には合計で10"
"個の単語とシンボルが含まれていることになります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Words-and-Symbols.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"However, if we mark the <code class=\"code\">multiply-by-seven</code> "
"definition with <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-M-h</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-"
"defun</code>), and then call <code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> "
"on it, we will find that <code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> "
"claims the definition has eleven words, not ten! Something is wrong!"
msgstr ""
"しかし、<code class=\"code\">multiply-by-seven</code> の定義に <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">C-M-h</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">mark-defun</code>) をマーク"
"し、その上で <code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> を呼び出すと、"
"<code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> がその定義には10語ではなく11"
"語あると主張していることがわかります！何かがおかしいです！"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Words-and-Symbols.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The problem is twofold: <code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> does "
"not count the &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; as a word, and it "
"counts the single symbol, <code class=\"code\">multiply-by-seven</code>, as "
"containing three words.  The hyphens are treated as if they were interword "
"spaces rather than intraword connectors: &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">multiply-by-seven</samp>&rsquo; is counted as if it were "
"written &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">multiply by seven</samp>&rsquo;."
msgstr ""
"問題は2点ある。<code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> は &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">*</samp>&rsquo; を単語としてカウントせず、単一の記号 "
"<code class=\"code\">multiply-by-seven</code> を3つの単語を含むものとしてカウ"
"ントする。ハイフンは単語内の連結要素ではなく、単語間のスペースであるかのよう"
"に扱われる。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">multiply-by-seven</samp>&rsquo; は、"
"あたかも &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">multiply by seven</samp>&rsquo; と書かれ"
"ているかのようにカウントされる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Words-and-Symbols.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The cause of this confusion is the regular expression search within the "
"<code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> definition that moves point "
"forward word by word.  In the canonical version of <code "
"class=\"code\">count-words-example</code>, the regexp is:"
msgstr ""
"この混乱の原因は、<code class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> の定義内に"
"ある、ポイントを単語単位で進める正規表現検索にあります。<code "
"class=\"code\">count-words-example</code> の正準版における正規表現は以下の通"
"りです："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/Words-and-Symbols.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "&quot;\\\\w+\\\\W*&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/Words-and-Symbols.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"This regular expression is a pattern defining one or more word constituent "
"characters possibly followed by one or more characters that are not word "
"constituents.  What is meant by &ldquo;word constituent characters&rdquo; "
"brings us to the issue of syntax, which is worth a section of its own."
msgstr ""
"この正規表現は、1つ以上の単語構成文字と、その後に続く可能性のある1つ以上の非"
"単語構成文字を定義するパターンです。「単語構成文字」が何を意味するのかという"
"点は構文の問題へとつながりますが、これについては別途一節を割く価値がありま"
"す。"

