#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><h3>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<span>7.1 <code class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</"
"code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#car-and-cdr\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span>7.1 <code class=\"code\">car</code> と <code class=\"code\">cdr</"
"code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#car-and-cdr\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of a list is, quite simply, the first "
"item in the list.  Thus the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of the list "
"<code class=\"code\">(rose violet daisy buttercup)</code> is <code "
"class=\"code\">rose</code>."
msgstr ""
"リストの<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>とは、端的に言えばリストの先頭要素のこ"
"とです。したがって、リスト<code class=\"code\">(rose violet daisy "
"buttercup)</code>の<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>は<code "
"class=\"code\">rose</code>となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If you are reading this in Info in GNU Emacs, you can see this by evaluating "
"the following:"
msgstr ""
"GNU EmacsのInfoでこれを読んでいる場合は、以下を実行することで確認できます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(car '(rose violet daisy buttercup))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"After evaluating the expression, <code class=\"code\">rose</code> will "
"appear in the echo area."
msgstr ""
"式を評価した後、echo領域に<code class=\"code\">rose</code>が表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">car</code> does not remove the first item from the "
"list; it only reports what it is.  After <code class=\"code\">car</code> has "
"been applied to a list, the list is still the same as it was.  In the "
"jargon, <code class=\"code\">car</code> is &ldquo;non-destructive&rdquo;.  "
"This feature turns out to be important."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">car</code> はリストから最初の項目を削除するわけではな"
"く、単にそれが何であるかを報告するだけです。<code class=\"code\">car</code> "
"をリストに適用した後も、リストは元のままです。専門用語で言えば、<code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> は「非破壊的」です。この特徴は重要であることがわか"
"ります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of a list is the rest of the list, that "
"is, the <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> function returns the part of the "
"list that follows the first item.  Thus, while the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</"
"small> of the list <code class=\"code\">'(rose violet daisy buttercup)</"
"code> is <code class=\"code\">rose</code>, the rest of the list, the value "
"returned by the <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> function, is <code "
"class=\"code\">(violet daisy buttercup)</code>."
msgstr ""
"リストの<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>はリストの残りの部分、すなわち<code "
"class=\"code\">cdr</code>関数はリストの最初の要素に続く部分を返します。した"
"がって、リスト<code class=\"code\">'(rose violet daisy buttercup)</code>の"
"<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>が<code class=\"code\">rose</code>であるのに対"
"し、リストの残りの部分である<code class=\"code\">cdr</code>関数が返す値は"
"<code class=\"code\">(violet daisy buttercup)</code>となります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "You can see this by evaluating the following in the usual way:"
msgstr "これは、以下を通常の方法で評価することで確認できます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(cdr '(rose violet daisy buttercup))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When you evaluate this, <code class=\"code\">(violet daisy buttercup)</code> "
"will appear in the echo area."
msgstr ""
"これを評価すると、エコー領域に <code class=\"code\">(violet daisy "
"buttercup)</code> が表示されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">car</code>, <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> does "
"not remove any elements from the list&mdash;it just returns a report of what "
"the second and subsequent elements are."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">car</code>と同様に、<code class=\"code\">cdr</code>はリ"
"ストから要素を削除するわけではなく、単に2番目以降の要素が何であるかというレ"
"ポートを返すだけです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Incidentally, in the example, the list of flowers is quoted.  If it were "
"not, the Lisp interpreter would try to evaluate the list by calling <code "
"class=\"code\">rose</code> as a function.  In this example, we do not want "
"to do that."
msgstr ""
"ちなみに、例では花のリストをクォートしています。  そうしないと、Lispインタプ"
"リタは <code class=\"code\">rose</code> を関数として呼び出してリストを評価し"
"ようとします。  この例では、そうしたことはしたくありません。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"For operating on lists, the names <code class=\"code\">first</code> and "
"<code class=\"code\">rest</code> would make more sense than the names <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</code>.  Indeed, some "
"programmers define <code class=\"code\">first</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">rest</code> as aliases for <code class=\"code\">car</code> "
"and <code class=\"code\">cdr</code>, then write <code class=\"code\">first</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">rest</code> in their code."
msgstr ""
"リストを操作する場合、<code class=\"code\">car</code>や<code "
"class=\"code\">cdr</code>という名称よりも、<code class=\"code\">first</code>"
"や<code class=\"code\">rest</code>という名称の方が理にかなっています。実際、"
"<code class=\"code\">first</code>や<code class=\"code\">rest</code>を<code "
"class=\"code\">car</code>や<code class=\"code\">cdr</code>のエイリアスとして"
"定義し、コード内で<code class=\"code\">first</code>や<code "
"class=\"code\">rest</code>と記述するプログラマーもいます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html
msgid ""
"However, lists in Lisp are built using a lower-level structure known as "
"&ldquo;cons cells&rdquo; (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-"
"Implementation.html\">How Lists are Implemented</a>), in which there is no "
"such thing as &ldquo;first&rdquo; or &ldquo;rest&rdquo;, and the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small> and the <small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> are "
"symmetrical.  Lisp does not try to hide the existence of cons cells, and "
"programs do use them for things other than lists.  For this reason, the "
"names are helpful for reminding programmers that <code class=\"code\">car</"
"code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> are in fact symmetrical, despite "
"the asymmetrical way they are used in lists."
msgstr ""
"しかし、Lispのリストは「コンスセル」と呼ばれる低レベルな構造を用いて構築され"
"ており（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-Implementation.html\">リストの実装方法"
"</a>を参照）、そこでは「先頭」や「末尾」といった概念はなく、<small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small>と<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small>は対称的です。Lispは"
"コンスセルの存在を隠そうとはしませんし、プログラムではリスト以外の用途でもこ"
"れらが利用されます。そのため、リスト内では非対称な使われ方をしているにもかか"
"わらず、<code class=\"code\">car</code>と<code class=\"code\">cdr</code>が実"
"際には対称的であることをプログラマに思い出させる上で、これらの名称は有用で"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When <code class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> are "
"applied to a list made up of symbols, such as the list <code "
"class=\"code\">(pine fir oak maple)</code>, the element of the list returned "
"by the function <code class=\"code\">car</code> is the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">pine</code> without any parentheses around it.  <code "
"class=\"code\">pine</code> is the first element in the list.  However, the "
"<small class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of the list is a list itself, <code "
"class=\"code\">(fir oak maple)</code>, as you can see by evaluating the "
"following expressions in the usual way:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">car</code> や <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> を、リス"
"ト <code class=\"code\">(pine fir oak maple)</code> のようなシンボルからなる"
"リストに適用すると、関数 <code class=\"code\">car</code> が返すリストの要素"
"は、括弧で囲まれていないシンボル <code class=\"code\">pine</code> となりま"
"す。<code class=\"code\">pine</code> はリストの最初の要素です。ただし、以下の"
"式を通常の方法で評価すればわかるように、このリストの <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> はそれ自体がリスト <code class=\"code\">(fir oak "
"maple)</code> となっています。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(car '(pine fir oak maple))\n"
"\n"
"(cdr '(pine fir oak maple))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"On the other hand, in a list of lists, the first element is itself a list.  "
"<code class=\"code\">car</code> returns this first element as a list.  For "
"example, the following list contains three sub-lists, a list of carnivores, "
"a list of herbivores and a list of sea mammals:"
msgstr ""
"一方、リストのリストでは、最初の要素自体がリストとなります。<code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> はこの最初の要素をリストとして返します。例えば、以"
"下のリストには、肉食動物のリスト、草食動物のリスト、海棲哺乳類のリストという3"
"つのサブリストが含まれています："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(car '((lion tiger cheetah)\n"
"       (gazelle antelope zebra)\n"
"       (whale dolphin seal)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In this example, the first element or <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of the "
"list is the list of carnivores, <code class=\"code\">(lion tiger cheetah)</"
"code>, and the rest of the list is <code class=\"code\">((gazelle antelope "
"zebra) (whale dolphin seal))</code>."
msgstr ""
"この例では、リストの最初の要素または<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>が肉食動物"
"のリスト<code class=\"code\">(lion tiger cheetah)</code>であり、リストの残り"
"の部分は<code class=\"code\">((gazelle antelope zebra) (whale dolphin "
"seal))</code>となっています。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(cdr '((lion tiger cheetah)\n"
"       (gazelle antelope zebra)\n"
"       (whale dolphin seal)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"It is worth saying again that <code class=\"code\">car</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">cdr</code> are non-destructive&mdash;that is, they do not "
"modify or change lists to which they are applied.  This is very important "
"for how they are used."
msgstr ""
"改めて述べておく価値がありますが、<code class=\"code\">car</code> と <code "
"class=\"code\">cdr</code> は非破壊的です。つまり、適用先のリストを変更したり"
"改変したりすることはありません。これは、これらの使い方において非常に重要な点"
"です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/car-_0026-cdr.html
msgid ""
"Also, in the first chapter, in the discussion about atoms, I said that in "
"Lisp, certain kinds of atom, such as an array, can be separated into parts; "
"but the mechanism for doing this is different from the mechanism for "
"splitting a list.  As far as Lisp is concerned, the atoms of a list are "
"unsplittable.  (See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Lisp-Atoms.html\">Lisp Atoms</"
"a>.)  The <code class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</"
"code> functions are used for splitting lists and are considered fundamental "
"to Lisp.  Since they cannot split or gain access to the parts of an array, "
"an array is considered an atom.  Conversely, the other fundamental function, "
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code>, can put together or construct a list, but "
"not an array.  (Arrays are handled by array-specific functions.  See <a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"elisp/Arrays.html#Arrays\">Arrays</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs "
"Lisp Reference Manual</cite>.)"
msgstr ""
"また、第1章のアトムに関する解説において、Lispでは配列などの特定の種類のアトム"
"を分割できると述べましたが、その仕組みはリストを分割する仕組みとは異なりま"
"す。Lispの観点からは、リストのアトムは分割不可能です。（<a class=\"xref\" "
"href=\"Lisp-Atoms.html\">Lispのアトム</a>を参照してください。）<code "
"class=\"code\">car</code>および<code class=\"code\">cdr</code>関数はリストの"
"分割に用いられ、Lispの基本機能とされています。これらの関数では配列を分割した"
"りその各要素にアクセスしたりすることができないため、配列はアトムとみなされま"
"す。逆に、もう一つの基本関数である<code class=\"code\">cons</code>は、リスト"
"を結合・構築することはできますが、配列は構築できません。（配列は配列専用の関"
"数で扱われます。<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</"
"cite>の<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/elisp/Arrays.html#Arrays\">配列</a>を参照してください。）"

