# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/cons.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-cons_002c-introduced\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-cons_002c-introduced\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/cons.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">cons</code> function constructs lists; it is the "
"inverse of <code class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</"
"code>.  For example, <code class=\"code\">cons</code> can be used to make a "
"four element list from the three element list, <code class=\"code\">(fir oak "
"maple)</code>:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code> 関数はリストを構築します。これは <code "
"class=\"code\">car</code> および <code class=\"code\">cdr</code> の逆関数で"
"す。例えば、<code class=\"code\">cons</code> を使えば、3要素のリスト <code "
"class=\"code\">(fir oak maple)</code> から4要素のリストを作成できます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/cons.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(cons 'pine '(fir oak maple))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/cons.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "After evaluating this list, you will see"
msgstr "このリストを確認すると、わかるでしょう"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/cons.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(pine fir oak maple)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/cons.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"appear in the echo area.  <code class=\"code\">cons</code> causes the "
"creation of a new list in which the element is followed by the elements of "
"the original list."
msgstr ""
"エコー領域に表示されます。<code class=\"code\">cons</code> を指定すると、要素"
"の後に元のリストの要素が続く新しいリストが作成されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/cons.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"We often say that <code class=\"code\">cons</code> puts a new element at the "
"beginning of a list, or that it attaches or pushes elements onto the list, "
"but this phrasing can be misleading, since <code class=\"code\">cons</code> "
"does not change an existing list, but creates a new one."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code> はリストの先頭に新しい要素を追加する、あるい"
"は要素をリストに付加したり押し込んだりする、とよく言いますが、この表現は誤解"
"を招く可能性があります。というのも、<code class=\"code\">cons</code> は既存の"
"リストを変更するのではなく、新しいリストを作成するからです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/cons.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Like <code class=\"code\">car</code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</code>, "
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code> is non-destructive."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">car</code>や<code class=\"code\">cdr</code>と同様に、"
"<code class=\"code\">cons</code>は非破壊的です。"

