# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/edebug.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Edebug is a source level debugger.  Edebug normally displays the source of "
"the code you are debugging, with an arrow at the left that shows which line "
"you are currently executing."
msgstr ""
"Edebugはソースレベルデバッガです。通常、デバッグ対象のコードのソースを表示"
"し、左側の矢印で現在どの行を実行しているかを示します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/edebug.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You can walk through the execution of a function, line by line, or run "
"quickly until reaching a <em class=\"dfn\">breakpoint</em> where execution "
"stops."
msgstr ""
"関数の実行を1行ずつ辿ることも、実行が停止する<em class=\"dfn\">ブレークポイン"
"ト</em>に到達するまで素早く実行することもできます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/edebug.html
msgid ""
"Edebug is described in <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/"
"software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Edebug.html#Edebug\">Edebug</a> in "
"<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>."
msgstr ""
"Edebugについては、<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</"
"cite>の<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/"
"manual/html_node/elisp/Edebug.html#Edebug\">Edebug</a>に記載されています。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/edebug.html
msgid ""
"Here is a bugged function definition for <code class=\"code\">triangle-"
"recursively</code>.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Recursive-triangle-"
"function.html\">Recursion in place of a counter</a>, for a review of it."
msgstr ""
"以下は <code class=\"code\">triangle-recursively</code> のバグのある関数定義"
"です。復習には <a class=\"xref\" href=\"Recursive-triangle-function.html\">カ"
"ウンタの代わりに再帰を用いる</a> を参照してください。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/edebug.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun triangle-recursively-bugged (number)\n"
"  &quot;Return sum of numbers 1 through NUMBER inclusive.\n"
"Uses recursion.&quot;\n"
"  (if (= number 1)\n"
"      1\n"
"    (+ number\n"
"       (triangle-recursively-bugged\n"
"        (1= number)))))               ; <span class=\"r\">Error here.</span>\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/edebug.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Normally, you would install this definition by positioning your cursor after "
"the function&rsquo;s closing parenthesis and typing <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-"
"e</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">eval-last-sexp</code>) or else by positioning "
"your cursor within the definition and typing <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-M-x</kbd> "
"(<code class=\"code\">eval-defun</code>).  (By default, the <code "
"class=\"code\">eval-defun</code> command works only in Emacs Lisp mode or in "
"Lisp Interaction mode.)"
msgstr ""
"通常、この定義をインストールするには、関数の閉じ括弧の後にカーソルを置いて "
"<kbd class=\"kbd\">C-x C-e</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">eval-last-sexp</"
"code>) と入力するか、あるいは定義の中にカーソルを置いて <kbd class=\"kbd\">C-"
"M-x</kbd> (<code class=\"code\">eval-defun</code>) と入力します。（デフォルト"
"では、<code class=\"code\">eval-defun</code> コマンドは Emacs Lisp モードまた"
"は Lisp Interaction モードでのみ動作します。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/edebug.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"However, to prepare this function definition for Edebug, you must first <em "
"class=\"dfn\">instrument</em> the code using a different command.  You can "
"do this by positioning your cursor within or just after the definition and "
"typing"
msgstr ""
