# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/forward_002dparagraph.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code> function moves point "
"forward to the end of the paragraph.  It is usually bound to <kbd "
"class=\"kbd\">M-}</kbd> and makes use of a number of functions that are "
"important in themselves, including <code class=\"code\">let*</code>, <code "
"class=\"code\">match-beginning</code>, and <code class=\"code\">looking-at</"
"code>."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code> 関数は、ポイントを段落の末尾ま"
"で進めます。通常は <kbd class=\"kbd\">M-}</kbd> にバインドされており、<code "
"class=\"code\">let*</code>、<code class=\"code\">match-beginning</code>、"
"<code class=\"code\">looking-at</code> など、それ自体が重要な複数の関数を利用"
"します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/forward_002dparagraph.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The function definition for <code class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code> is "
"considerably longer than the function definition for <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> because it works with a paragraph, "
"each line of which may begin with a fill prefix."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code> の関数定義が <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> の関数定義よりもかなり長いのは、これが"
"段落を対象としており、各行がフィルプレフィックスで始まる可能性があるためで"
"す。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/forward_002dparagraph.html
msgid ""
"A fill prefix consists of a string of characters that are repeated at the "
"beginning of each line.  For example, in Lisp code, it is a convention to "
"start each line of a paragraph-long comment with &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">;;; </samp>&rsquo;.  In Text mode, four blank spaces make up "
"another common fill prefix, creating an indented paragraph.  (See <a data-"
"manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"emacs/Fill-Prefix.html#Fill-Prefix\">Fill Prefix</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>, for more information about fill "
"prefixes.)"
msgstr ""
"フィルプレフィックスとは、各行の先頭に繰り返し記述される文字列のことです。例"
"えば、Lispコードでは、段落形式のコメントの各行を &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">;;; </samp>&rsquo; で始めるのが慣習となっています。テキスト"
"モードでは、4つの空白文字がもう一つの一般的なフィルプレフィックスとなり、イン"
"デントされた段落を作成します。（フィルプレフィックスの詳細については、<cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite> の <a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/emacs/Fill-"
"Prefix.html#Fill-Prefix\">Fill Prefix</a> を参照してください。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/forward_002dparagraph.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The existence of a fill prefix means that in addition to being able to find "
"the end of a paragraph whose lines begin on the left-most column, the <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-paragraph</code> function must be able to find the "
"end of a paragraph when all or many of the lines in the buffer begin with "
"the fill prefix."
msgstr ""
"フィルプレフィックスが存在するということは、<code class=\"code\">forward-"
"paragraph</code> 関数が、行が最左列から始まる段落の末尾を特定できるだけでな"
"く、バッファ内のすべての行、あるいは多くの行がフィルプレフィックスで始まる場"
"合に、その段落の末尾を特定できなければならないことを意味します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/forward_002dparagraph.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Moreover, it is sometimes practical to ignore a fill prefix that exists, "
"especially when blank lines separate paragraphs.  This is an added "
"complication."
msgstr ""
"さらに、特に空行で段落が区切られている場合には、存在するフィルプレフィックス"
"を無視するのが実用的なこともある。これはさらなる複雑さをもたらす。"

