# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-kill_002dappend\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-kill_002dappend\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "The <code class=\"code\">kill-append</code> function looks like this:"
msgstr "<code class=\"code\">kill-append</code> 関数は次のようになります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun kill-append (string before-p &amp;optional yank-handler)\n"
"  &quot;Append STRING to the end of the latest kill in the kill ring.\n"
"If BEFORE-P is non-nil, prepend STRING to the kill.\n"
"... &quot;\n"
"  (let* ((cur (car kill-ring)))\n"
"    (kill-new (if before-p (concat string cur) (concat cur string))\n"
"              (or (= (length cur) 0)\n"
"                  (equal yank-handler\n"
"                         (get-text-property 0 'yank-handler cur)))\n"
"              yank-handler)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">kill-append</code> function is fairly "
"straightforward.  It uses the <code class=\"code\">kill-new</code> function, "
"which we will discuss in more detail in a moment."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">kill-append</code> 関数はかなりシンプルです。この関数は "
"<code class=\"code\">kill-new</code> 関数を利用しており、これについては後ほど"
"詳しく説明します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"(Also, the function provides an optional argument called <code "
"class=\"code\">yank-handler</code>; when invoked, this argument tells the "
"function how to deal with properties added to the text, such as bold or "
"italics.)"
msgstr ""
"（また、この関数には <code class=\"code\">yank-handler</code> というオプショ"
"ン引数が用意されており、これを指定すると、太字や斜体などテキストに追加された"
"プロパティをどのように処理すべきかを関数に伝えることができます。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"It has a <code class=\"code\">let*</code> function to set the value of the "
"first element of the kill ring to <code class=\"code\">cur</code>.  (I do "
"not know why the function does not use <code class=\"code\">let</code> "
"instead; only one value is set in the expression.  Perhaps this is a bug "
"that produces no problems?)"
msgstr ""
"キルリングの最初の要素の値を<code class=\"code\">cur</code>に設定する<code "
"class=\"code\">let*</code>関数があります。（なぜ代わりに<code "
"class=\"code\">let</code>を使わないのかは分かりません。式内で設定される値は1"
"つだけです。おそらく、特に問題は生じないバグなのでしょうか？）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Consider the conditional that is one of the two arguments to <code "
"class=\"code\">kill-new</code>.  It uses <code class=\"code\">concat</code> "
"to concatenate the new text to the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> of the "
"kill ring.  Whether it prepends or appends the text depends on the results "
"of an <code class=\"code\">if</code> expression:"
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">kill-new</code> の2つの引数のうちの1つである条件式を考え"
"てみましょう。この条件式は <code class=\"code\">concat</code> を用いて、新し"
"いテキストをキルリングの <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> に連結します。テキス"
"トを先頭に付加するか末尾に付加するかは、<code class=\"code\">if</code> 式の結"
"果によって決まります："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(if before-p                            ; <span class=\"r\">if-part</span>\n"
"    (concat string cur)                 ; <span class=\"r\">then-part</span>\n"
"  (concat cur string))                  ; <span class=\"r\">else-part</span>\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If the region being killed is before the region that was killed in the last "
"command, then it should be prepended before the material that was saved in "
"the previous kill; and conversely, if the killed text follows what was just "
"killed, it should be appended after the previous text.  The <code "
"class=\"code\">if</code> expression depends on the predicate <code "
"class=\"code\">before-p</code> to decide whether the newly saved text should "
"be put before or after the previously saved text."
msgstr ""
"削除対象の領域が、直前のコマンドで削除された領域よりも前にある場合は、前回の"
"削除時に保存された内容の前に付加されるべきであり、逆に、削除対象のテキストが"
"直前に削除された内容の後に続く場合は、前回のテキストの後に付加されるべきで"
"す。<code class=\"code\">if</code> 式は、新たに保存されたテキストを前回保存さ"
"れたテキストの前に置くか後に置くかを決定するために、述語 <code "
"class=\"code\">before-p</code> に依存します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The symbol <code class=\"code\">before-p</code> is the name of one of the "
"arguments to <code class=\"code\">kill-append</code>.  When the <code "
"class=\"code\">kill-append</code> function is evaluated, it is bound to the "
"value returned by evaluating the actual argument.  In this case, this is the "
"expression <code class=\"code\">(&lt; end beg)</code>.  This expression does "
"not directly determine whether the killed text in this command is located "
"before or after the kill text of the last command; what it does is determine "
"whether the value of the variable <code class=\"code\">end</code> is less "
"than the value of the variable <code class=\"code\">beg</code>.  If it is, "
"it means that the user is most likely heading towards the beginning of the "
"buffer.  Also, the result of evaluating the predicate expression, <code "
"class=\"code\">(&lt; end beg)</code>, will be true and the text will be "
"prepended before the previous text.  On the other hand, if the value of the "
"variable <code class=\"code\">end</code> is greater than the value of the "
"variable <code class=\"code\">beg</code>, the text will be appended after "
"the previous text."
msgstr ""
"記号 <code class=\"code\">before-p</code> は、<code class=\"code\">kill-"
"append</code> の引数の一つの名前です。<code class=\"code\">kill-append</"
"code> 関数が評価される際、それは実引数を評価して得られた値にバインドされま"
"す。この場合、その値は式 <code class=\"code\">(&lt; end beg)</code> となりま"
"す。この式は、このコマンドで削除されたテキストが、直前のコマンドで削除された"
"テキストの前にあるか後にあるかを直接的に判定するものではありません。この式が"
"行うのは、変数 <code class=\"code\">end</code> の値が変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">beg</code> の値よりも小さいかどうかを判定することです。もし小"
"さい場合、ユーザーはバッファの先頭に向かっている可能性が高いことを意味しま"
"す。また、述語式 <code class=\"code\">(&lt; end beg)</code> の評価結果は "
"true となり、テキストは直前のテキストの前に付加されます。一方、変数 <code "
"class=\"code\">end</code> の値が変数 <code class=\"code\">beg</code> の値より"
"も大きい場合、テキストは直前のテキストの後に付加されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"When the newly saved text will be prepended, then the string with the new "
"text will be concatenated before the old text:"
msgstr ""
"新しく保存されたテキストが先頭に付加される場合、新しいテキストを含む文字列が"
"元のテキストの前に連結されます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(concat string cur)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"But if the text will be appended, it will be concatenated after the old text:"
msgstr "ただし、テキストが追記される場合は、既存のテキストの後に連結されます："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(concat cur string))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"To understand how this works, we first need to review the <code "
"class=\"code\">concat</code> function.  The <code class=\"code\">concat</"
"code> function links together or unites two strings of text.  The result is "
"a string.  For example:"
msgstr ""
"この仕組みを理解するために、まずは<code class=\"code\">concat</code>関数につ"
"いて確認しましょう。<code class=\"code\">concat</code>関数は、2つのテキスト文"
"字列を連結または結合します。その結果は1つの文字列となります。例えば："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(concat &quot;abc&quot; &quot;def&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;abcdef&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(concat &quot;new &quot;\n"
"        (car '(&quot;first element&quot; &quot;second element&quot;)))\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;new first element&quot;\n"
"\n"
"(concat (car\n"
"        '(&quot;first element&quot; &quot;second element&quot;)) &quot; modified&quot;)\n"
"     &rArr; &quot;first element modified&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"We can now make sense of <code class=\"code\">kill-append</code>: it "
"modifies the contents of the kill ring.  The kill ring is a list, each "
"element of which is saved text.  The <code class=\"code\">kill-append</code> "
"function uses the <code class=\"code\">kill-new</code> function which in "
"turn uses the <code class=\"code\">setcar</code> function."
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dappend-function.html
msgid ""
"<span class=\"nav-button\"><span class=\"nav-label\">Next: </span><span "
"class=\"nav-link\"><a href=\"kill_002dnew-function.html\">The <code "
"class=\"code\">kill-new</code> function</a></span></span>, <span class=\"nav-"
"button\"><span class=\"nav-label\">Previous: </span><span class=\"nav-"
"link\"><a href=\"last_002dcommand-_0026-this_002dcommand.html\"><code "
