msgid ""
"As explained in the previous chapter (see <a class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-"
"Implementation.html\">How Lists are Implemented</a>), the computer does not "
"keep two different copies of the text being pointed to by both the <code "
"class=\"code\">kill-ring</code> and the <code class=\"code\">kill-ring-yank-"
"pointer</code>.  The words &ldquo;a different piece of text&rdquo; and "
"&ldquo;yet more text&rdquo; are not duplicated.  Instead, the two Lisp "
"variables point to the same pieces of text.  Here is a diagram:"
msgstr ""
"前章で説明した通り（<a class=\"pxref\" href=\"List-Implementation.html\">リス"
"トの実装方法</a>を参照）、コンピュータは<code class=\"code\">kill-ring</code>"
"と<code class=\"code\">kill-ring-yank-pointer</code>の両方が指し示すテキスト"
"のコピーを2つ保持しているわけではありません。「別のテキスト部分」や「さらに別"
"のテキスト部分」といった表現が重複して存在するわけではないのです。むしろ、2つ"
"のLisp変数は同じテキスト部分を指しています。以下に図を示します："

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Attribute 'alt' of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><div><img>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dring_002dyank_002dpointer.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "cons-5"
msgstr "cons-5"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dring_002dyank_002dpointer.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Both the variable <code class=\"code\">kill-ring</code> and the variable "
"<code class=\"code\">kill-ring-yank-pointer</code> are pointers.  But the "
"kill ring itself is usually described as if it were actually what it is "
"composed of.  The <code class=\"code\">kill-ring</code> is spoken of as if "
"it were the list rather than that it points to the list.  Conversely, the "
"<code class=\"code\">kill-ring-yank-pointer</code> is spoken of as pointing "
"to a list."
msgstr ""
"変数 <code class=\"code\">kill-ring</code> と変数 <code class=\"code\">kill-"
"ring-yank-pointer</code> はいずれもポインタである。しかし、キルリング自体は、"
"通常、実際にそれが構成されている実体であるかのように記述される。<code "
"class=\"code\">kill-ring</code> は、リストを指しているのではなく、それ自体が"
"リストであるかのように語られる。逆に、<code class=\"code\">kill-ring-yank-"
"pointer</code> はリストを指しているものとして語られる。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><br><br><p>
#: build/html/eintr/kill_002dring_002dyank_002dpointer.html
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"These two ways of talking about the same thing sound confusing at first but "
"make sense on reflection.  The kill ring is generally thought of as the "
"complete structure of data that holds the information of what has recently "
"been cut out of the Emacs buffers.  The <code class=\"code\">kill-ring-yank-"
"pointer</code> on the other hand, serves to indicate&mdash;that is, to point "
"to&mdash;that part of the kill ring of which the first element (the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CAR</small>) will be inserted."
msgstr ""
"同じものについて語るこれら2つの表現は、一見すると紛らわしく感じられますが、よ"
"く考えれば納得がいきます。キルリングは一般的に、最近Emacsバッファから切り出さ"
"れた情報を保持するデータ構造全体のことと考えられています。一方、<code "
"class=\"code\">kill-ring-yank-pointer</code>は、キルリングのどの部分に最初の"
"要素（<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>）が挿入されるかを示す――つまり、そこを指"
"し示す――役割を果たします。"

