msgstr ""
"<span>3.6 <code class=\"code\">let</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" "
"href=\"#let-1\"> &para;</a></span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/let.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-let\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-let\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/let.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">let</code> expression is a special form in Lisp "
"that you will need to use in most function definitions."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> という式は Lisp の特殊な形式であり、ほとんど"
"の関数定義で使用する必要があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/let.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> is used to attach or bind a symbol to a "
"value in such a way that the Lisp interpreter will not confuse the variable "
"with a variable of the same name that is not part of the function."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">let</code> は、Lispインタプリタが変数を、関数の一部では"
"ない同名の変数と混同しないように、シンボルを値に紐付けたりバインドしたりする"
"ために使用されます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/let.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"To understand why the <code class=\"code\">let</code> special form is "
"necessary, consider the situation in which you own a home that you generally "
"refer to as &ldquo;the house&rdquo;, as in the sentence, &ldquo;The house "
"needs painting.&rdquo; If you are visiting a friend and your host refers to "
"&ldquo;the house&rdquo;, he is likely to be referring to <em "
"class=\"emph\">his</em> house, not yours, that is, to a different house."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">let</code>という特殊形式がなぜ必要なのかを理解するため"
"に、「その家は塗り替えが必要だ」という文のように、普段「その家」と呼んでいる"
"自宅を持っている状況を考えてみてください。友人を訪ねている際、ホストが「その"
"家」と言った場合、それはあなたの家ではなく<em class=\"emph\">彼の</em>家、つ"
"まり別の家を指している可能性が高いでしょう。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/let.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"If your friend is referring to his house and you think he is referring to "
"your house, you may be in for some confusion.  The same thing could happen "
"in Lisp if a variable that is used inside of one function has the same name "
"as a variable that is used inside of another function, and the two are not "
"intended to refer to the same value.  The <code class=\"code\">let</code> "
"special form prevents this kind of confusion."
msgstr ""
"友人が自分の家のことを指しているのに、あなたが自分の家のことを指していると"
"思っている場合、混乱が生じるかもしれません。Lispにおいても、ある関数内で使用"
"される変数が、別の関数内で使用される変数と同じ名前であり、かつその2つが同じ値"
"を指す意図ではない場合に、同様のことが起こり得ます。<code "
"class=\"code\">let</code> 特殊形式は、こうした混乱を防ぎます。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><ul><li>
#: build/html/eintr/let.html
msgid ""
