#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><h4>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"<span>An explanation of <code class=\"code\">nil</code><a class=\"copiable-"
"link\" href=\"#An-explanation-of-nil\"> &para;</a></span>"
msgstr ""
"<span><code class=\"code\">nil</code><a class=\"copiable-link\" href=\"#An-"
"explanation-of-nil\"> &para;</a> の解説</span>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Before illustrating a test for truth, we need an explanation of <code "
"class=\"code\">nil</code>."
msgstr ""
"真理性の検定を例示する前に、<code class=\"code\">nil</code>についての説明が必"
"要である。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In Emacs Lisp, the symbol <code class=\"code\">nil</code> has two meanings.  "
"First, it means the empty list.  Second, it means false and is the value "
"returned when a true-or-false-test tests false.  <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> can be written as an empty list, <code class=\"code\">()</code>, or as "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code>.  As far as the Lisp interpreter is "
"concerned, <code class=\"code\">()</code> and <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> are the same.  Humans, however, tend to use <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> for false and <code class=\"code\">()</code> for the empty list."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispにおいて、シンボル <code class=\"code\">nil</code> には2つの意味が"
"あります。1つ目は空リストを意味します。2つ目は false を意味し、真偽判定テスト"
"が false となった際に返される値です。<code class=\"code\">nil</code> は、空リ"
"スト、<code class=\"code\">()</code>、あるいは <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code> として記述できます。Lispインタプリタの観点からは、<code "
"class=\"code\">()</code> と <code class=\"code\">nil</code> は同じものです。"
"しかし、人間は false に <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を、空リストに <code "
"class=\"code\">()</code> を用いる傾向があります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In Emacs Lisp, any value that is not <code class=\"code\">nil</"
"code>&mdash;is not the empty list&mdash;is considered true.  This means that "
"if an evaluation returns something that is not an empty list, an <code "
"class=\"code\">if</code> expression will test true.  For example, if a "
"number is put in the slot for the test, it will be evaluated and will return "
"itself, since that is what numbers do when evaluated.  In this conditional, "
"the <code class=\"code\">if</code> expression will test true.  The "
"expression tests false only when <code class=\"code\">nil</code>, an empty "
"list, is returned by evaluating the expression."
msgstr ""
"Emacs Lispでは、<code class=\"code\">nil</code>（空リストではない）あらゆる値"
"は真とみなされます。つまり、評価の結果が空リストではない値となった場合、"
"<code class=\"code\">if</code> 式は真と判定されます。例えば、テスト用のスロッ"
"トに数値が格納されている場合、その数値は評価され、数値が評価された際の挙動に"
"従って自身を返します。この条件式において、<code class=\"code\">if</code> 式は"
"真と判定されます。この式が偽と判定されるのは、式の評価によって空リストである "
"<code class=\"code\">nil</code> が返された場合のみです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You can see this by evaluating the two expressions in the following examples."
msgstr "次の例で2つの式を評価すれば、それが分かります。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"In the first example, the number 4 is evaluated as the test in the <code "
"class=\"code\">if</code> expression and returns itself; consequently, the "
"then-part of the expression is evaluated and returned: &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">true</samp>&rsquo; appears in the echo area.  In the second "
"example, the <code class=\"code\">nil</code> indicates false; consequently, "
"the else-part of the expression is evaluated and returned: &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">false</samp>&rsquo; appears in the echo area."
msgstr ""
"最初の例では、<code class=\"code\">if</code> 式のテストとして数値 4 が評価さ"
"れ、自身を返します。その結果、式の then 部分が評価されて返され、エコー領域に "
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">true</samp>&rsquo; が表示されます。2番目の例で"
"は、<code class=\"code\">nil</code> は偽を示します。その結果、式の else 部分"
"が評価されて返され、エコー領域に &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">false</"
"samp>&rsquo; が表示されます。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(if 4\n"
"    'true\n"
"  'false)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(if nil\n"
"    'true\n"
"  'false)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Incidentally, if some other useful value is not available for a test that "
"returns true, then the Lisp interpreter will return the symbol <code "
"class=\"code\">t</code> for true.  For example, the expression <code "
"class=\"code\">(&gt; 5 4)</code> returns <code class=\"code\">t</code> when "
"evaluated, as you can see by evaluating it in the usual way:"
msgstr ""
"ちなみに、真を返すテストに対して他に有用な値が用意されていない場合、Lispイン"
"タプリタは真を表すシンボル <code class=\"code\">t</code> を返します。例えば、"
"式 <code class=\"code\">(&gt; 5 4)</code> は、通常の方法で評価すればわかるよ"
"うに、評価時に <code class=\"code\">t</code> を返します："

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "(&gt; 5 4)\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nil-explained.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"On the other hand, this function returns <code class=\"code\">nil</code> if "
"the test is false."
msgstr ""
"一方、この関数はテストが偽の場合に <code class=\"code\">nil</code> を返しま"
"す。"

