# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-nth\"></a>"
msgstr "<a class=\"index-entry-id\" id=\"index-nth\"></a>"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">nthcdr</code> function takes the <small "
"class=\"sc\">CDR</small> of a list repeatedly.  The <code "
"class=\"code\">nth</code> function takes the <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> "
"of the result returned by <code class=\"code\">nthcdr</code>.  It returns "
"the Nth element of the list."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">nthcdr</code> 関数は、リストの <small class=\"sc\">CDR</"
"small> を繰り返し取得します。<code class=\"code\">nth</code> 関数は、<code "
"class=\"code\">nthcdr</code> が返す結果の <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> を"
"取得します。そして、リストの N 番目の要素を返します。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Thus, if it were not defined in C for speed, the definition of <code "
"class=\"code\">nth</code> would be:"
msgstr ""
"したがって、速度向上のためにC言語で定義されていない場合、<code "
"class=\"code\">nth</code>の定義は次のようになります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(defun nth (n list)\n"
"  &quot;Returns the Nth element of LIST.\n"
"N counts from zero.  If LIST is not that long, nil is returned.&quot;\n"
"  (car (nthcdr n list)))\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"(Originally, <code class=\"code\">nth</code> was defined in Emacs Lisp in "
"<samp class=\"file\">subr.el</samp>, but its definition was redone in C in "
"the 1980s.)"
msgstr ""
"（もともと <code class=\"code\">nth</code> は Emacs Lisp では <samp "
"class=\"file\">subr.el</samp> で定義されていたが、1980年代に C 言語で定義が書"
"き直された。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"The <code class=\"code\">nth</code> function returns a single element of a "
"list.  This can be very convenient."
msgstr ""
"<code class=\"code\">nth</code> 関数は、リストの単一の要素を返します。これは"
"非常に便利です。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Note that the elements are numbered from zero, not one.  That is to say, the "
"first element of a list, its <small class=\"sc\">CAR</small> is the zeroth "
"element.  This zero-based counting often bothers people who are accustomed "
"to the first element in a list being number one, which is one-based."
msgstr ""
"なお、要素の番号は1ではなく0から始まる点に注意してください。つまり、リストの"
"最初の要素である<small class=\"sc\">CAR</small>が0番目の要素となります。この"
"ような0始まりの数え方は、リストの最初の要素が1番であることに慣れている人々（1"
"始まりに慣れている人々）にとって、しばしば違和感の原因となります。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(nth 0 '(&quot;one&quot; &quot;two&quot; &quot;three&quot;))\n"
"    &rArr; &quot;one&quot;\n"
"\n"
"(nth 1 '(&quot;one&quot; &quot;two&quot; &quot;three&quot;))\n"
"    &rArr; &quot;two&quot;\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/nth.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"It is worth mentioning that <code class=\"code\">nth</code>, like <code "
"class=\"code\">nthcdr</code> and <code class=\"code\">cdr</code>, does not "
"change the original list&mdash;the function is non-destructive.  This is in "
"sharp contrast to the <code class=\"code\">setcar</code> and <code "
"class=\"code\">setcdr</code> functions."
msgstr ""
"なお、<code class=\"code\">nth</code>は<code class=\"code\">nthcdr</code>や"
"<code class=\"code\">cdr</code>と同様に元のリストを変更しません。つまり、この"
"関数は非破壊的です。これは、<code class=\"code\">setcar</code>や<code "
"class=\"code\">setcdr</code>の関数とは対照的です。"

