# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Sometimes when you you write text, you duplicate words&mdash;as with "
"&ldquo;you you&rdquo; near the beginning of this sentence.  I find that most "
"frequently, I duplicate &ldquo;the&rdquo;; hence, I call the function for "
"detecting duplicated words, <code class=\"code\">the-the</code>."
msgstr ""
"文章を書いていると、この文の冒頭にある「you you」のように、単語を重ねてしまう"
"ことがあります。特に「the」を重ねてしまうことが多いため、重複単語を検出する関"
"数を<code class=\"code\">the-the</code>と名付けました。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"As a first step, you could use the following regular expression to search "
"for duplicates:"
msgstr "まずは、以下の正規表現を使って重複を検索してみるとよいでしょう。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\\\(\\\\w+[ \\t\\n]+\\\\)\\\\1\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><hr><p>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html
msgid ""
"This regexp matches one or more word-constituent characters followed by one "
"or more spaces, tabs, or newlines.  However, it does not detect duplicated "
"words on different lines, since the ending of the first word, the end of the "
"line, is different from the ending of the second word, a space.  (For more "
"information about regular expressions, see <a class=\"ref\" href=\"Regexp-"
"Search.html\">Regular Expression Searches</a>, as well as <a data-"
"manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"emacs/Regexps.html#Regexps\">Syntax of Regular Expressions</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>, and <a data-manual=\"elisp\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/elisp/Regular-"
"Expressions.html#Regular-Expressions\">Regular Expressions</a> in <cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>.)"
msgstr ""
"この正規表現は、1つ以上の単語構成文字に続き、1つ以上のスペース、タブ、または"
"改行にマッチします。ただし、1つ目の単語の末尾である行末と、2つ目の単語の末尾"
"であるスペースとは異なるため、異なる行にある重複した単語は検出されません。"
"（正規表現の詳細については、<a class=\"ref\" href=\"Regexp-Search.html\">正規"
"表現検索</a>のほか、<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>の<a "
"data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/"
"html_node/emacs/Regexps.html#Regexps\">正規表現の構文</a>、および<cite "
"class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>の<a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_node/"
"elisp/Regular-Expressions.html#Regular-Expressions\">正規表現</a>を参照してく"
"ださい。）"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"You might try searching just for duplicated word-constituent characters but "
"that does not work since the pattern detects doubles such as the two "
"occurrences of &ldquo;th&rdquo; in &ldquo;with the&rdquo;."
msgstr ""
"単語を構成する文字の重複だけを検索してみるのもいいかもしれませんが、それでは"
"うまくいきません。というのも、パターンが &ldquo;with the&rdquo; 内の "
"&ldquo;th&rdquo; の2箇所のような重複を検出してしまうからです。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Another possible regexp searches for word-constituent characters followed by "
"non-word-constituent characters, reduplicated.  Here, &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\\\w+</samp>&rsquo; matches one or more word-constituent "
"characters and &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\W*</samp>&rsquo; matches zero "
"or more non-word-constituent characters."
msgstr ""
"もう一つの候補となる正規表現は、単語構成文字に続いて非単語構成文字が出現する"
"パターンを、繰り返し検索するものです。ここでは、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\\\w+</samp>&rsquo;が1つ以上の単語構成文字に、&lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">\\\\W*</samp>&rsquo;が0個以上の非単語構成文字にそれぞれマッチ"
"します。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\\\(\\\\(\\\\w+\\\\)\\\\W*\\\\)\\\\1\n"
msgstr ""

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid "Again, not useful."
msgstr "やっぱり、役に立たない。"

# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#.  /@w 
#.  /@w 
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Here is the pattern that I use.  It is not perfect, but good enough.  &lsquo;"
"<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\b</samp>&rsquo; matches the empty string, provided "
"it is at the beginning or end of a word; &lsquo;<samp "
"class=\"samp\">[^@&nbsp;\\n\\t]+</samp>&rsquo; matches one or more "
"occurrences of any characters that are <em class=\"emph\">not</em> an @-"
"sign, space, newline, or tab."
msgstr ""
"私が使っているパターンはこちらです。完璧ではありませんが、十分使えます。"
"&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">\\\\b</samp>&rsquo;は、単語の先頭または末尾にある"
"場合に限り、空文字列にマッチします。&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">[^@&nbsp;"
"\\n\\t]+</samp>&rsquo;は、@記号、スペース、改行、またはタブ<em "
"class=\"emph\">ではない</em>任意の文字が1回以上出現する場合にマッチします。"

#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><div><pre>
#: build/html/eintr/the_002dthe.html build/html/mono/eintr.html
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\\\b\\\\([^@ \\n\\t]+\\\\)[ \\n\\t]+\\\\1\\\\b\n"
msgstr ""

