# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Regular expression searches are described in <a data-manual=\"emacs\" "
"href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_mono/emacs.html#Regexp-"
"Search\">Regular Expression Search</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs "
"Manual</cite>, as well as in <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://"
"www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_mono/elisp.html#Regular-"
"Expressions\">Regular Expressions</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs "
"Lisp Reference Manual</cite>.  In writing this chapter, I am presuming that "
"you have at least a mild acquaintance with them.  The major point to "
"remember is that regular expressions permit you to search for patterns as "
"well as for literal strings of characters.  For example, the code in <code "
"class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> searches for the pattern of possible "
"characters that could mark the end of a sentence, and moves point to that "
"spot."
msgstr "正規表現による検索については、<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"emacs\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_mono/emacs.html#Regexp-Search\">正規表現検索</a>、および<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>の<a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_mono/elisp.html#Regular-Expressions\">正規表現</a>で解説されています。本章を執筆するにあたり、読者の皆様がこれらについて少なくともある程度の知識をお持ちであることを前提としています。特に留意すべき点は、正規表現を用いることで、リテラルな文字列だけでなく、パターンの検索も可能になるということです。例えば、<code class=\"code\">forward-sentence</code> のコードは、文末を示す可能性のある文字のパターンを検索し、ポイントをその位置に移動させます。"

