#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"We are already familiar with <code class=\"code\">setq</code>.  We use a "
"similar macro <code class=\"code\">setq-default</code> to set the following "
"variable, <code class=\"code\">major-mode</code><a class=\"footnote\" "
"id=\"DOCF20\" href=\"#FOOT20\"><sup>20</sup></a>, to the subsequent value, "
"which is <code class=\"code\">text-mode</code>.  The single-quote before "
"<code class=\"code\">text-mode</code> tells Emacs to deal directly with the "
"<code class=\"code\">text-mode</code> symbol, not with whatever it might "
"stand for.  See <a class=\"xref\" href=\"#setq\">Setting the Value of a "
"Variable</a>, for a reminder of how <code class=\"code\">setq</code> works.  "
"The main point is that there is no difference between the procedure you use "
"to set a value in your <samp class=\"file\">.emacs</samp> file and the "
"procedure you use anywhere else in Emacs."
msgstr ""

