# Machine-translated by PLaMo Translate.
#. type: Content of: <html><body><div><br><br><br><br><br><hr><div><hr><div><hr><div><p>
#: build/html/mono/eintr.html
msgid ""
"Blank spaces are inserted using the <code class=\"code\">make-string</code> "
"function.  This function takes two arguments: the first tells it how long "
"the string will be and the second is a symbol for the character to insert, "
"in a special format.  The format is a question mark followed by a blank "
"space, like this, &lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">? </samp>&rsquo;.  See <a data-"
"manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_mono/"
"elisp.html#Character-Type\">Character Type</a> in <cite class=\"cite\">The "
"GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite>, for a description of the syntax for "
"characters.  (Of course, you might want to replace the blank space by some "
"other character &hellip; You know what to do.)"
msgstr "空白は <code class=\"code\">make-string</code> 関数を用いて挿入されます。この関数は2つの引数を取ります。1つ目は文字列の長さを、2つ目は特殊な形式の挿入文字を表す記号を指定します。形式は、&lsquo;<samp class=\"samp\">? </samp>&rsquo; のように、クエスチョンマークに続いて空白が入るものです。文字の構文に関する説明については、<cite class=\"cite\">The GNU Emacs Lisp Reference Manual</cite> の <a data-manual=\"elisp\" href=\"https://www.gnu.org/software/emacs/manual/html_mono/elisp.html#Character-Type\">Character Type</a> を参照してください。（もちろん、空白を別の文字に置き換えたい場合もあるでしょう……やり方はお分かりかと思います。）"

